-- ── Bài 8: Bad Choices (chữ từ audio bằng Whisper, đã soát; có POV và Commentary) ──
insert into public.effortless_lessons (course, lesson_no, slug, title, level, description, cover, main_audio, ms_audio, vocab_audio,
  pov_audio, com_audio, main_story, mini_story, ms_parts, pov_story, com_story, vocab, patterns, phrases)
values (
  'Original Course', 8, 'bad-choices', 'Bad Choices', 'intermediate',
  'Một bà mẹ đơn thân viết thư cho bác sĩ Tracy vì bạn trai mới vẫn qua lại với vợ cũ. Học cách nói về các mối quan hệ, sự nghi ngờ và lựa chọn — kèm POV luyện thì và lời bình của A.J.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581998392741-67879e0ef04a',
  'Original_Course/108a Bad Choices (main).mp3',
  'Original_Course/108c Bad Choices (ms).mp3',
  'Original_Course/108b Bad Choices (vocabulary).mp3',
  'Original_Course/108d Bad Choices (pov).mp3',
  'Original_Course/108e Bad Choices (com).mp3',
  $j$[[0.5, "Bad Choices", "Những lựa chọn sai lầm"], [3.8, "Dear Dr. Tracy, I am a 33-year-old divorced woman with four kids.", "Thưa bác sĩ Tracy, tôi là một phụ nữ 33 tuổi đã ly hôn và có bốn đứa con."], [10.2, "I was married for 12 years and have been divorced for approximately three years.", "Tôi đã kết hôn 12 năm và ly hôn được khoảng ba năm."], [15.4, "I met my new boyfriend during my divorce.", "Tôi gặp bạn trai mới trong lúc đang ly hôn."], [18.5, "We hit it off and have been together ever since.", "Chúng tôi hợp nhau ngay và ở bên nhau từ đó đến giờ."], [21.7, "He is a 44-year-old divorced man.", "Anh ấy 44 tuổi và cũng đã ly hôn."], [25.2, "When I met him, he had been divorced for two years.", "Khi tôi gặp anh ấy, anh ấy đã ly hôn được hai năm."], [28.7, "Well, I met his ex-wife, and she seemed to be an okay person.", "Tôi có gặp vợ cũ của anh ấy, và cô ta có vẻ là người cũng được."], [33.7, "What I found out three months into my relationship with him was that he was fooling around with his ex-wife again, who also at this time had a boyfriend of her own.", "Điều tôi phát hiện ra sau ba tháng quen anh ấy là anh ấy lại đang lăng nhăng với vợ cũ, trong khi lúc đó cô ta cũng đã có bạn trai riêng."], [43.8, "I figured that since I did not have a committed relationship with him, I had no place to say anything.", "Tôi nghĩ vì giữa chúng tôi chưa có cam kết gì nên tôi không có quyền lên tiếng."], [50.4, "The problem is, it continued further into our relationship, up to the point when I found out I was pregnant.", "Vấn đề là chuyện đó vẫn tiếp diễn khi chúng tôi đã gắn bó hơn, cho đến lúc tôi phát hiện mình có thai."], [57.1, "At the same time, I found out that he and his ex-wife planned to go to his family reunion together.", "Cùng lúc đó, tôi biết được anh ấy và vợ cũ định cùng nhau đi dự buổi họp mặt gia đình của anh ấy."], [63.8, "Of course, before all of this, I drove by his house one night and saw her car parked outside his home.", "Tất nhiên, trước tất cả chuyện này, có một đêm tôi lái xe ngang nhà anh ấy và thấy xe của cô ta đậu bên ngoài."], [71.6, "The excuse I got after all of this was that they were considering getting back together.", "Lời bào chữa tôi nhận được sau tất cả là họ đang tính chuyện quay lại với nhau."], [76.7, "I thought it was very funny that as soon as she met me, she found interest in him again.", "Tôi thấy thật buồn cười là ngay khi gặp tôi, cô ta lại thấy hứng thú với anh ấy."], [83.3, "I guess my issue is the fact that I am now still in this relationship.", "Tôi đoán vấn đề của tôi là việc giờ tôi vẫn còn ở trong mối quan hệ này."], [88.9, "I have brought a child into this nonsense, and I hate the fact that he keeps in contact with her.", "Tôi đã sinh một đứa con trong mớ hỗn độn này, và tôi ghét việc anh ấy vẫn giữ liên lạc với cô ta."], [94.3, "My boyfriend has taken responsibility for her son from a previous relationship.", "Bạn trai tôi đã nhận trách nhiệm với đứa con trai của cô ta từ một mối quan hệ trước."], [99.7, "His excuse for having so much contact with his ex-wife is because of that boy.", "Anh ấy viện cớ liên lạc nhiều với vợ cũ là vì cậu bé đó."], [104.8, "I know this is not true, but I have no real proof otherwise.", "Tôi biết điều đó không đúng, nhưng tôi không có bằng chứng thật sự nào để chứng minh."], [108.4, "I have also dealt with him taking women to hotels, and my gut tells me it was her.", "Tôi cũng đã phải chịu đựng chuyện anh ấy đưa phụ nữ vào khách sạn, và linh cảm mách bảo tôi đó là cô ta."], [114.5, "But he promises it was not her.", "Nhưng anh ấy hứa rằng không phải cô ta."], [116.6, "I have tried to get over all the cheating.", "Tôi đã cố vượt qua mọi chuyện phản bội."], [118.8, "I know that she is very close to his family, and I also know that his family does not like me because I stand up for myself.", "Tôi biết cô ta rất thân với gia đình anh ấy, và tôi cũng biết gia đình anh ấy không ưa tôi vì tôi dám lên tiếng bảo vệ mình."], [126.7, "I guess the bottom line is knowing how much contact his ex-wife has with him and the fact that he knows that I can't stand her.", "Tôi đoán điều cốt lõi là việc biết vợ cũ liên lạc với anh ấy nhiều đến mức nào, trong khi anh ấy biết tôi không chịu nổi cô ta."], [134.4, "Am I in a weird relationship with a man that wants to have his cake and eat it too?", "Có phải tôi đang ở trong một mối quan hệ kỳ quặc với một người đàn ông muốn “được cả chì lẫn chài”?"], [139.1, "Or am I being paranoid and need to just trust him when he says he does not want her?", "Hay tôi đang đa nghi quá và chỉ cần tin anh ấy khi anh ấy nói không cần cô ta?"], [146.0, "I have never had so much animosity towards two people in my life.", "Cả đời tôi chưa từng căm ghét hai người nào đến thế."], [150.4, "I do love this man, but I feel like I have put myself back in an unhealthy relationship with a man that is trying to lie to me.", "Tôi thật lòng yêu người đàn ông này, nhưng tôi cảm thấy mình lại tự đặt mình vào một mối quan hệ không lành mạnh với một người đang cố nói dối tôi."], [158.3, "To be totally honest, now that I have his child, I even hate the fact that he helps her son.", "Thành thật mà nói, giờ tôi đã có con với anh ấy, tôi thậm chí ghét cả việc anh ấy giúp đỡ con trai cô ta."], [164.3, "She never has to ask for anything regarding that boy, but I have to constantly remind him when our son needs something.", "Cô ta chẳng bao giờ phải xin gì cho cậu bé đó, còn tôi thì phải liên tục nhắc anh ấy mỗi khi con trai chúng tôi cần gì."], [170.9, "He does it for the other boy without thinking, but my son is a second thought.", "Anh ấy lo cho cậu bé kia mà chẳng cần suy nghĩ, còn con trai tôi thì chỉ được nghĩ tới sau."], [176.0, "Even when I have said, “Look at your son, he is in dire need.”", "Ngay cả khi tôi đã nói: “Nhìn con trai anh đi, nó đang rất cần anh.”"], [180.6, "I was married to a cheating man and hooked up with another cheating man.", "Tôi đã cưới một người đàn ông ngoại tình, rồi lại cặp với một người đàn ông ngoại tình khác."], [184.6, "I wonder if it's just my bad choices in men.", "Tôi tự hỏi có phải chỉ là do tôi chọn đàn ông sai lầm."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.3, "s", "Welcome to the mini-story for Bad Choices."], [4.4, "s", "Let's get started with the story."], [7.2, "s", "David Beckham is a man who wants to have his cake and eat it too."], [14.1, "s", "He wants to be a famous movie star and a famous football player."], [20.1, "s", "So he moves to Hollywood."], [22.4, "s", "He hooks up with Tom Cruise."], [25.2, "s", "They hit it off immediately."], [27.5, "s", "David likes Tom."], [28.9, "s", "Tom likes David."], [30.3, "s", "Beckham says, “The bottom line is that I want to be a movie star just like you, Tom.”"], [34.4, "s", "“Can you help me?”"], [36.0, "s", "Tom says, “Of course, my gut tells me you will be a big success in Hollywood.”"], [42.8, "s", "So Tom introduces Beckham to a director who is very powerful."], [48.4, "s", "The director makes a movie with Beckham."], [51.6, "s", "But it's a terrible movie, everybody hates it and they hate Beckham."], [56.8, "s", "The public feels a powerful animosity towards Beckham."], [61.4, "s", "They can't stand him."], [63.3, "s", "They yell at him."], [64.4, "s", "They throw things at him."], [66.6, "s", "Beckham can't deal with the public's animosity."], [69.5, "s", "He is a guy who is very sensitive."], [71.8, "s", "He becomes scared."], [73.2, "s", "He feels this is a dire situation."], [76.8, "s", "Beckham is so scared he won't leave his house."], [80.0, "s", "He keeps the windows closed and the doors locked."], [83.5, "s", "He becomes paranoid."], [84.6, "s", "And he won't leave the house even to play soccer."], [89.5, "s", "Finally, his team manager calls and says, This is a situation which is unacceptable."], [95.4, "s", "You're fired!"], [97.4, "s", "Beckham cries, No!"], [100.0, "s", "He has no job and nobody can stand him."], [105.5, "s", "Okay, let's go back to the top."], [108.2, "s", "This time with questions."], [110.6, "s", "David Beckham is a man who wants to have his cake and eat it too."], [116.8, "q", "Does Beckham want two things, but really he can only have one?"], [123.2, "a", "Yes, that's the exact meaning of to have his cake and eat it too."], [127.0, "s", "What does he want?"], [127.7, "q", "What two things does he want?"], [128.9, "a", "Well, he wants to be a soccer player and a movie star."], [133.1, "s", "He wants both, but actually he must choose."], [136.6, "s", "He can only be one, either a movie star or a soccer player."], [142.3, "s", "He doesn't have enough time or talent or skill to do both."], [147.0, "s", "But he wants both."], [148.4, "s", "He wants to have his cake and eat it too."], [152.8, "q", "Does Beckham want to have his cake and eat it too by being rich and good looking?"], [162.6, "a", "Well, no, actually no."], [164.1, "s", "It's possible to be rich and good looking."], [167.1, "s", "That's okay."], [167.7, "s", "You can look good."], [168.6, "s", "You can be handsome and rich."], [170.9, "s", "You don't need to choose between those two things."], [174.3, "s", "So that's not the problem."], [175.7, "s", "He wants to have his cake and eat it too."], [178.2, "s", "Because he wants to be a famous soccer player and be a famous actor at the same time."], [186.0, "s", "And this is not possible."], [187.6, "s", "He wants to have his cake and eat it too."], [189.9, "s", "He wants both things but he can only have one."], [193.3, "s", "So he moves to Hollywood."], [194.6, "s", "He hooks up with Tom Cruise."], [196.8, "q", "Does he meet Tom Cruise?"], [199.9, "a", "Yes, he does."], [200.6, "s", "He meets Tom Cruise."], [202.2, "q", "Does he hook up with John Travolta?"], [205.9, "a", "No, he doesn't hook up with John Travolta."], [208.4, "q", "Does he hook up with Julia Roberts?"], [211.4, "a", "No, he doesn't hook up with Julia Roberts."], [213.9, "q", "Does he hook up with Tom Cruise?"], [216.6, "a", "Yes, he does, of course."], [218.3, "q", "Does he hook up with Julia Roberts or Tom Cruise?"], [222.9, "a", "Well, he hooks up with Tom Cruise."], [227.0, "q", "Does he hook up with the Spice Girls?"], [229.7, "a", "Well, in the past he hooked up with one of the Spice Girls, right?"], [234.4, "s", "He hooked up with one of the Spice Girls."], [237.4, "s", "Now, this is a different meaning of “hooked up”."], [240.4, "q", "Is he dating Tom Cruise?"], [242.1, "a", "Well, no, he's not."], [243.4, "s", "He hooked up with Tom Cruise means he just met Tom Cruise."], [247.5, "s", "They met, they got together."], [249.2, "s", "But if he hooked up with one of the Spice Girls, then that means, yeah, he's dating her."], [255.2, "s", "He's married to her now, etc."], [257.6, "s", "So he hooked up with Tom Cruise, and they hit it off immediately."], [262.6, "q", "Did Tom hate David?"], [266.7, "a", "No, no."], [267.5, "s", "They hit it off immediately."], [269.2, "s", "They liked each other immediately."], [272.2, "q", "Did Beckham hit it off with Tom?"], [276.4, "a", "Yes, he did."], [277.6, "s", "Beckham liked Tom."], [278.8, "q", "Did Tom hit it off with Beckham?"], [281.8, "a", "Yeah, Tom also liked Beckham."], [284.2, "s", "They hit it off."], [284.8, "s", "They both hit it off."], [287.7, "q", "Did Tom Cruise hit it off with Ronaldinho?"], [293.1, "a", "No, no."], [293.9, "s", "He didn't hit it off with Ronaldinho."], [295.3, "s", "In fact, he hates Ronaldinho."], [297.1, "s", "He hates him."], [298.4, "s", "He likes Beckham because Beckham is cool and he looks good."], [303.0, "s", "So he hit it off with David Beckham."], [305.4, "s", "He did not hit it off with Ronaldinho."], [308.6, "q", "Who did Beckham hit it off with?"], [313.6, "a", "Well, he hit it off with Tom Cruise."], [317.1, "s", "Alright, so they liked each other."], [319.3, "s", "And Beckham said."], [320.8, "s", "The bottom line, Tom, is that I want to be a movie star just like you."], [327.7, "q", "What is Beckham's final point, his most important point?"], [332.7, "a", "Well, the most important thing he wants is to be a movie star just like Tom Cruise."], [337.9, "s", "That's the bottom line."], [339.1, "q", "Is the bottom line that Beckham wants money?"], [345.3, "a", "No, that's not the bottom line."], [347.4, "s", "Money is not the most important thing for Beckham right now."], [351.3, "q", "What is the bottom line for David Beckham?"], [354.5, "a", "The bottom line is he wants to be a famous movie star."], [358.2, "s", "That's his bottom line."], [359.9, "s", "That's his main point, his final point, his most important point."], [364.6, "q", "What is Tom Cruise's bottom line?"], [368.4, "a", "Well, maybe Tom Cruise's bottom line is Scientology, his religion."], [372.6, "s", "That's his bottom line."], [373.7, "s", "He wants to get David to join Scientology, to join his religion."], [378.8, "s", "That's Tom's secret bottom line."], [381.4, "s", "But Beckham's bottom line is that he wants to be a movie star."], [384.9, "s", "So he says, the bottom line is, I want to be a movie star just like you."], [390.9, "s", "Tom Cruise says, of course, my gut tells me you will be a big success in Hollywood."], [397.8, "q", "Does Tom know, definitely, 100% that Beckham will succeed?"], [405.2, "a", "No, no, he doesn't know, not in his brain, not in his mind."], [409.0, "s", "His gut tells him that he will be a big success."], [412.6, "s", "He has a feeling, right?"], [414.7, "s", "A feeling in his stomach."], [415.8, "s", "He has a deep feeling that Beckham will be successful, but he doesn't really know."], [421.6, "s", "He's not sure."], [422.7, "s", "He just has a strong feeling."], [425.9, "s", "His gut tells him that Beckham will be a big success in Hollywood."], [431.3, "q", "Does his gut tell him that Beckham will be a great soccer player in Los Angeles?"], [437.1, "a", "No, his gut does not tell him he will be a great soccer player."], [441.6, "q", "What does Tom's gut tell him?"], [445.4, "a", "Tom's gut tells him that Beckham will be a big success in Hollywood as an actor."], [451.8, "s", "His gut doesn't tell him that he'll be a big success as a soccer player."], [456.3, "s", "Maybe he won't be."], [458.0, "s", "But his gut tells him that he'll be a big success in Hollywood."], [462.7, "q", "Whose gut tells him that Beckham will succeed?"], [468.7, "a", "Well, Tom Cruise's gut tells him that Beckham will be a big success in Hollywood."], [474.7, "s", "And so, Tom introduces Beckham to a director who is very powerful."], [480.4, "s", "The director makes a movie with Beckham."], [483.2, "s", "But, it's a terrible movie."], [486.1, "s", "Everybody hates it, and they hate Beckham too."], [489.4, "s", "The public feels a powerful animosity towards Beckham."], [494.3, "q", "Does the public like David Beckham?"], [497.5, "a", "No, they feel animosity towards him."], [501.1, "q", "Do they think Beckham is their enemy?"], [504.4, "a", "Yes, that's right, they think David Beckham is their enemy."], [508.0, "s", "He is the enemy of goodness."], [510.0, "s", "He is the enemy of good quality."], [512.4, "s", "He is the enemy of honesty."], [514.3, "s", "He is their enemy."], [515.4, "s", "They feel a powerful animosity towards him."], [518.8, "s", "They feel animosity towards Beckham."], [521.8, "q", "Who feels animosity towards Beckham?"], [526.7, "a", "Well, the public, the American public feels animosity towards Beckham."], [531.9, "q", "Does Tom Cruise feel animosity towards Beckham?"], [537.5, "a", "No, no."], [538.2, "s", "Tom still likes David Beckham."], [539.8, "s", "Tom does not feel animosity towards Beckham."], [542.9, "s", "The public feels animosity towards Beckham."], [546.7, "q", "Does Beckham feel animosity towards the public?"], [551.9, "a", "No."], [553.3, "s", "Beckham loves the public."], [554.5, "s", "He wants them to love him."], [557.0, "s", "The public feels animosity towards Beckham."], [559.2, "s", "But Beckham does not feel animosity towards the public."], [565.4, "s", "So the public feels animosity towards Beckham."], [568.1, "s", "They can't stand him."], [570.3, "q", "Do they love him?"], [572.6, "