ow she wants a divorce, because Beckham is not famous anymore."], [925.0, "s", "Nobody likes him, so his wife wants a divorce."], [928.3, "s", "She can't stand him."], [929.8, "s", "Tom Cruise can't stand him."], [931.4, "s", "His coach can't stand him."], [933.4, "s", "The public can't stand him."], [935.7, "s", "Nobody likes him."], [937.1, "s", "Okay, this one is a little long, so no time to pause."], [941.6, "s", "So what I would like you to do, go back."], [944.0, "s", "Listen to each sentence."], [945.9, "s", "Then pause and repeat the sentence."], [948.5, "s", "Copy my pronunciation."], [950.5, "s", "Then listen to the next sentence."], [951.8, "s", "Pause again."], [953.9, "s", "Repeat my pronunciation."], [955.7, "s", "Copy my pronunciation."], [957.3, "s", "And then play one more sentence, and then pause."], [960.4, "s", "And again."], [961.7, "s", "Copy my pronunciation."], [964.6, "s", "After you do that, finally try to tell all of the story yourself."], [970.8, "s", "Okay, go on to the Point of View mini-stories next."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.3, "Hello, welcome to the POV, Point of View, mini-stories for Bad Choices."], [6.9, "Same story, different time."], [8.8, "Let's start the first one with three years ago."], [13.3, "We'll have to imagine this happened three years ago."], [17.4, "Three years ago, David Beckham was a man who wanted to have his cake and eat it too."], [23.0, "He wanted to be a famous movie star and a famous soccer player at the same time."], [31.2, "So he moved to Hollywood."], [32.5, "He hooked up with Tom Cruise."], [34.8, "They hit it off immediately."], [37.4, "Tom liked David."], [39.0, "David liked Tom."], [41.7, "Beckham said, Tom, the bottom line is that I want to be a movie star just like you."], [47.6, "Can you help me?"], [48.3, "Tom said, of course, my gut tells me you'll be a big success in Hollywood."], [55.3, "So Tom introduced Beckham to a director who was very powerful."], [60.2, "The director made a movie with Beckham."], [62.9, "But it was a terrible movie."], [65.1, "Everybody hated it, and they hated Beckham."], [68.4, "The public felt a powerful animosity towards Beckham."], [72.6, "They couldn't stand him."], [74.5, "They yelled at him and threw things at him."], [76.8, "Beckham couldn't deal with the public's animosity."], [81.7, "He was a guy who was very sensitive."], [84.5, "So he became scared."], [86.3, "He felt this was a dire situation."], [90.0, "Beckham was so scared he wouldn't leave his house."], [93.3, "He kept the windows closed and the doors locked."], [96.8, "He became paranoid and wouldn't even leave to play soccer."], [100.9, "Finally, his team manager said, this is a situation which is unacceptable."], [107.4, "You're fired."], [109.4, "Beckham cried."], [111.0, "He had no job and nobody could stand him."], [117.3, "Alright, let's change the time a little bit."], [120.0, "This time we're going to talk about the story, but that Beckham has always wanted to do these things, okay?"], [128.3, "So these have been happening for a while."], [131.7, "Beckham has always been a man who has wanted to have his cake and eat it, too."], [139.9, "He has always wanted to be a famous movie star and a famous football player."], [145.7, "He has always wanted to move to Hollywood."], [149.4, "He has always wanted to hook up with Tom Cruise."], [153.5, "And he has hoped they would hit it off immediately."], [157.3, "David has always liked Tom Cruise."], [160.5, "Tom has always liked David."], [163.5, "Well, one day, Beckham said,"], [166.2, "Look Tom, the bottom line is that I want to be a movie star, just like you."], [170.8, "Can you help me?"], [172.3, "Tom said, “Of course, my gut tells me you will be a big success in Hollywood.”"], [177.8, "So Tom introduced Beckham to a director who was very powerful."], [181.9, "The director made a movie with Beckham."], [183.7, "But it was a terrible movie."], [186.7, "Everybody hated it and they hated Beckham."], [189.2, "The public felt a powerful animosity towards Beckham."], [193.0, "They couldn't stand him."], [194.7, "They yelled at him."], [195.8, "They threw things at him."], [198.0, "Beckham couldn't deal with the public's animosity."], [201.6, "He was a guy who was very sensitive."], [203.7, "He has always been a guy who was very sensitive."], [206.9, "He felt this was a dire situation."], [210.5, "Beckham was so scared he wouldn't leave his house."], [213.4, "He kept the windows closed and the doors locked."], [216.6, "He became paranoid and wouldn't even leave to play soccer."], [222.2, "Finally his team manager called and said, this is a situation which is unacceptable."], [227.6, "You're fired."], [229.9, "Beckham cried."], [231.0, "He had no job and nobody could stand him."], [235.2, "Okay, you'll notice that I use the perfect, the have been, have gone, that verb tense."], [242.8, "When I was talking about things that have always been true or that were true for a while in the past, maybe starting in the past until now, or maybe over some time in the past, a range of time."], [256.6, "And then when I talked about specific conversations, specific actions, I used the simple past."], [266.9, "Alright, don't think about that too much."], [269.3, "Listening is how you will improve your grammar, listening and practicing."], [273.1, "Why is not a good question about grammar or language."], [277.2, "Don't ask why."], [280.5, "If you want a PhD, a doctorate in linguistics, you can ask why."], [285.1, "If you want to be fluent, if you want to speak English easily and naturally, don't ask why, okay?"], [291.7, "Just learn it."], [292.8, "Just listen carefully."], [293.8, "Just do the lessons."], [295.3, "You will improve, I promise."], [297.0, "All right, next, let's talk about the future."], [299.8, "In fact, maybe this is gonna be a true story, right?"], [303.7, "Let's think, what's going to happen to David Beckham when he comes to Hollywood?"], [308.6, "He's moving to Los Angeles."], [310.0, "That's true."], [311.0, "What's going to happen?"], [311.9, "Let's imagine."], [312.6, "This is what I think will happen."], [314.6, "So now, the future."], [316.4, "Next year, David Beckham is moving to Los Angeles."], [323.0, "And he is a man who wants to have his cake and eat it too."], [328.2, "I think he will want to be a famous movie star and a famous football player at the same time."], [335.7, "That's why he's moving to Hollywood."], [338.8, "He's gonna hook up with Tom Cruise."], [341.4, "They'll hit it off."], [343.0, "David will like Tom."], [344.5, "Tom will like David."], [346.9, "Beckham will say to Tom, “The bottom line is, I want to be a movie star just like you.”"], [352.9, "Can you help me?"], [354.2, "Tom will say, of course, my gut tells me you are gonna be a big success in Hollywood."], [361.4, "So, Tom will introduce Beckham to a director who will be very powerful."], [367.0, "The director will make a movie with Beckham, but it's going to be a terrible movie."], [373.0, "Everybody will hate it, and they'll hate Beckham too."], [376.6, "The public will feel a powerful animosity towards Beckham."], [380.4, "They won't be able to stand him."], [382.8, "They'll yell at him and throw things at him."], [385.3, "Beckham won't be able to deal with the public's animosity."], [391.9, "He's a guy who is very sensitive, so he'll be scared."], [396.6, "He'll feel this is a dire situation."], [400.6, "Beckham will be so scared he won't leave his house."], [404.2, "He'll keep the windows closed and the doors locked."], [407.2, "He'll become paranoid, and he won't even leave to play soccer."], [412.7, "Finally, his team manager will call and say, this is a situation which is unacceptable."], [419.1, "You're fired."], [421.2, "Beckham will cry."], [422.6, "He'll have no job and nobody will be able to stand him."], [428.4, "All right, did you notice in the future, when we're talking about the future."], [433.2, "We say we'll be able to instead of can, right?"], [437.2, "Instead of can stand him, I'll say we'll be able to stand him in the future."], [441.4, "And you'll also, in the future, you have to listen very carefully."], [446.0, "Because in real speech."], [447.9, "Not textbooks, but real American English, we add “'ll” to the subject, right?"], [455.0, "Beckham'll do this, Beckham'll do that."], [458.6, "Now in a textbook, you will see Beckham will go to Los Angeles."], [464.0, "But we say, Beckham'll, Beckham'll — the “'ll” gives you the future."], [468.4, "Beckham will go to Los Angeles."], [471.4, "And in the textbook, you'll see “going to”: Beckham is going to make a movie."], [479.1, "But in real speech, we say “gonna”."], [482.6, "Beckham's gonna, right?"], [484.1, "We don't say “Beckham is going to”."], [487.7, "We say “Beckham's gonna”."], [489.7, "Beckham's gonna make a movie."], [492.2, "Beckham's gonna do this, Beckham's gonna do that."], [496.3, "Beckham'll go."], [497.4, "Beckham'll come."], [498.5, "So we use “gonna” and “'ll” for the future in real speech."], [503.3, "That's how we actually say it when we speak."], [505.6, "So listen carefully for that."], [507.2, "Listen very carefully when you hear those future versions."], [510.9, "Now please go back."], [511.9, "Listen to each version."], [513.6, "Pause after the version."], [515.1, "Tell it yourself."], [516.6, "Try to tell it yourself."], [517.7, "If you can't, it's okay."], [519.8, "Relax."], [520.4, "Rewind, listen again."], [521.0, "Rewind, listen again, every day."], [521.9, "It's not a race."], [522.7, "Just relax, enjoy it."], [523.4, "Okay, see you next time."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.0, "Welcome to the commentary for bad choices."], [5.6, "I actually used this letter, this Dr. Tracey letter, in my class here in San Francisco, and we chatted about this topic a little bit."], [16.0, "And what we talked about was the question."], [18.8, "Why do people make the same bad choices again and again and again?"], [24.8, "So for example, at the bottom of the letter, she says, I was married to a cheating man, her first husband."], [32.3, "And then she said, I hooked up with another cheating man."], [35.4, "And I wonder, is it just my bad choices in men?"], [39.0, "And you know, there are a lot of people like this."], [42.7, "When I was a social worker, for example, before I became a teacher,"], [47.2, "I had this kind of client all the time."], [51.1, "I'll give you the very strong example."], [53.6, "Some women always, always date men who abuse them, who hurt them, who hit them."], [61.1, "And it happens again and again and again."], [65.1, "So they date one man, and the man, you know, hits them, and finally they leave this man."], [73.4, "The next guy, the next guy they date, after a few months, maybe after six months or seven months, he starts to hit them."], [82.1, "And then they stay with him for a long time."], [85.7, "They break up, and then again they're really not happy."], [89.4, "And they finally find another guy."], [91.5, "He seems so nice."], [93.0, "You meet him, he seems very polite."], [95.5, "But guess what happens?"], [97.0, "Six months, seven months later, he also abuses her, hits her."], [101.0, "And it was a serious question."], [103.2, "That's a very serious situation, obviously."], [105.3, "And I would always ask, you know, what's happening here?"], [109.0, "Why are they choosing the same kind of guy again and again and again?"], [114.0, "And of course, we all do this sometimes."], [116.9, "I think most of us have something in our life that's not working right, that never works."], [123.1, "There's just some part of our life, and we continue to make the same bad choices again and again and again."], [130.7, "My personal example, a small example, is eating sugar."], [134.0, "I always eat chocolate and bad stuff, and I know it's bad for me, and I try to stop eating it."], [140.4, "But then every night I go and I eat some more chocolate."], [144.1, "And then I'll say, “No, this is bad, I shouldn't do this.”"], [147.7, "And then, you know, maybe I'll try one week to be healthy, and I only eat good food."], [153.2, "And then finally, oh, I get some chocolate again, or I get something sweet."], [157.5, "So this is my own thing, and of course,"], [160.2, "with me, there's some physical part too; it's a little bit of a sugar addiction."], [164.4, "But a lot of us have these kind of behaviors in our life."], [168.5, "And it happens a lot in relationships."], [170.7, "People choose other people who have a similar problem."], [175.7, "And it repeats again and again and again and again."], [178.9, "And you know, it's not always conscious."], [180.8, "Sometimes people would get angry at the women, for example, when I was a social worker."], [185.0, "Why do these women do this?"], [186.2, "Why do they always choose these men, you know, and they blame the woman?"], [192.1, "And of course it is happening."], [193.6, "The woman is doing this."], [194.5, "She is choosing these men, but it's usually unconscious."], [198.1, "Okay."], [198.5, "The woman is not thinking."], [199.4, "“Oh, I want to find a man who hits me.”"], [201.7, "Of course not, they don't want that, but there's something unconscious."], [207.1, "Possibly something from their childhood, their own parents, some experiences."], [212.9, "Possibly something else, that they unconsciously are attracted to something about these men."], [219.8, "And also these men are attracted to something about them, or about these kind of women."], [226.8, "And it usually has kind of a deep psychological root."], [230.4, "It's not just so simple as, oh, why do they do this?"], [233.9, "They don't realize they're doing it, or they realize it, but they don't know why it's happening."], [239.4, "So it's quite serious and it really is a very serious problem and some women do break that."], [246.4, "Now some women will, if they have an abusive boyfriend who hurts them, it's not this kind of situation."], [253.7, "Sometimes they have one and they say, oh never again and they never again date someone like that."], [260.7, "Because you know men who are like this."], [262.8, "It's not like in the beginning they're always very sweet and polite."], [267.4, "I worked at a shelter for women who were abused."], [271.1, "So at this house, we would let the women and the children come and live in the house to escape the men."], [279.1, "We helped them find a job and helped them find another place away from the man."], [285.0, "And you know, I got to hear a lot of stories about these men, and I even met some of them."], [292.7, "And you know, the thing about them is they're almost always very sweet and romantic."], [298.2, "In fact, even more than normal."], [301.1, "If you meet them just the first time, hi, how are you?"], [304.2, "Many times they seem like they're just so great."], [307.8, "Wow, they're so nice, they're so romantic."], [310.8, "And when the women first date them, these men are like always saying super nice things and giving them gifts."], [318.6, "Lots and lots of attention."], [321.6, "And then slowly, a little bit later, after they date longer, they start to control a little bit more."], [328.6, "Right?"], [329.0, "They don't like the woman's friends, so they try to make the woman get rid of her friends."], [335.8, "And then they separate the woman from her family."], [338.0, "They want just the woman and him, just them, nobody else."], [342.7, "So the woman becomes more isolated, more alone, only with the man."], [346.8, "And then finally, after many months, the man might hit her the first time."], [352.7, "It doesn't happen in the beginning right away."], [354.9, "So these women are not stupid, you know, it's hard to know sometimes."], [359.6, "But anyway, there is some kind of dynamic."], [361.8, "Some kind of psychological thing happening."], [365.4, "Where why do they keep getting with these kind of men?"], [369.9, "I think more personally, we might think about, and maybe you could write about in the forums."], [375.4, "Think about what kind of problems do you have in your life that keep happening again and again?"], [381.8, "Somehow you unconsciously are choosing this kind of situation or you're making it worse."], [389.6, "You know, I've mentioned my sugar problem as an example, and it just keeps happening again and again, no matter what I do."], [398.0, "And Tomoe yells at me and tells me to stop doing that, right?"], [401.8, "She's shaking her head yes."], [404.0, "So think about that."], [405.3, "Why do you continue to make bad choices sometimes in your life?"], [410.4, "And what bad choices do you usually make?"], [412.4, "What parts of your life do you do this?"], [415.1, "And why do you think this is happening?"], [417.8, "Now later I'm going to do a lesson with an article by a man named Bill Ferguson."], [424.8, "And he actually, the article, he actually has a few articles about this exact topic."], [430.7, "And he talks about why people do this."], [433.8, "And, even better, he talks about how you can solve this kind of problem."], [438.6, "How you can break the cycle."], [440.2, "You can break the pattern and stop making these choices again and again."], [444.8, "Very interesting."], [446.0, "His name is Bill Ferguson."], [447.6, "Do a Google search for him."], [449.5, "Bill, B-I-L-L."], [451.1, "And Ferguson is his last name."], [452.9, "I'm trying to remember how to spell Ferguson."], [455.5, "But anyway, this guy was a very interesting guy."], [458.6, "He was a divorce lawyer."], [460.4, "So he was helping people get divorced."], [464.4, "But he didn't like it."], [466.2, "He didn't like it because all the people were just fighting all the time."], [470.6, "And he thought that he should try to help people have a better relationship."], [475.2, "So instead of helping people just get divorced and fight, he started trying to help people talk and figure out their problems."], [486.1, "So if they did get a divorce, they would be friends."], [491.5, "They could have a calm breakup, basically, and they wouldn't hate each other."], [497.9, "There wouldn't be all these terrible, angry, nasty, negative emotions."], [502.8, "And when he started to do this,"], [506.3, "it started to work."], [507.3, "He was helping a lot of people, so he decided to become a counselor."], [511.0, "I think he was on Oprah's TV show a few times."], [514.2, "Anyway, go to his website."], [516.8, "His name is Bill Ferguson, B-I-L-L."], [520.2, "And his last name is F-E-R-G-U-S-O-N, Bill Ferguson."], [526.4, "His website is called Mastery of Life, so it's www.MasteryOfLife.com, so www.M-A-S-T-E-R-Y-O-F-L-I-F-E.com."], [544.6, "Mastery of Life, three words together."], [547.6, "Anyway, he's got some interesting articles on there, and I will use some of his articles for a future lesson."], [554.4, "All right, so that's all."], [555.4, "Go to the forums, try to write a little bit."], [557.8, "Write about this topic."], [559.0, "What should this woman do?"], [561.2, "Write about your own life."], [562.9, "What problems do you have in your life that happen again and again?"], [566.4, "Alright, I'll see you next time."], [567.9, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb
)
