  $j$[[0.8, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for Double Standard."], [4.7, "Now, this letter caused some interesting discussions in my San Francisco class."], [11.5, "And there were two main topics."], [13.3, "One topic was the topic of families and individuals."], [18.6, "And the other topic was double standards for men and women."], [22.1, "And I'll talk about both of these and a little bit about what's common in America, common opinions in America, and what are some of the different ideas in different countries."], [36.1, "So first this topic of family and individuals."], [39.7, "Most people know that American culture, American society, values individualism or individuals."], [47.7, "And we have an idea that adult individuals should make their own choices."], [54.3, "And they should not worry about what other people think, even their families."], [59.5, "And as you get older, this becomes stronger and stronger."], [64.0, "So when I read this letter, for example."], [67.3, "And I saw this woman is in her mid-50s, middle 50s, so she's probably, you know, 55 years old."], [74.0, "And she's worried about what her family thinks about her new boyfriend."], [81.2, "My first reaction, I thought, this is very strange."], [83.8, "This is an older woman."], [85.2, "Why does she care about what her sister and her parents think?"], [89.2, "She should just do what she wants."], [91.1, "She's an adult woman."], [92.7, "This is crazy."], [94.3, "And that's a common American reaction."], [96.4, "We have an idea in the United States that when you're an adult you should be independent."], [103.0, "You should make your own decisions."], [104.9, "You should not ask your parents for advice all the time."], [108.9, "You should not live with your parents when you're an adult."], [112.6, "Right?"], [112.8, "That's a very common strong view."], [116.9, "This is very interesting because in classes that I've had before, there's a very interesting difference in culture here."], [125.6, "Especially this idea of living with your family."], [129.8, "Some cultures, people continue to live with their families until they get married."], [135.6, "So if they're 30 and they're not married, they still live with their parents."], [140.1, "If they're 35 and they're not married, they're still living with their parents, and that's normal."], [145.3, "Which is fine."], [147.0, "There's not a right or wrong answer here, nothing better or worse, but it is a big difference."], [151.7, "In the United States, that is seen as very negative."], [156.0, "There's a strong feeling that you should not live with your parents when you're an adult."], [162.6, "So for example, in my own life, I went to university when I was 18."], [168.4, "And then I graduated university, I was 20, 22, I believe."], [173.4, "And after that, I got my own apartment, and I never lived with my parents again."], [178.8, "I didn't want to live with my parents."], [180.4, "And my parents did not want me to live with them."], [184.6, "If I had asked them, can I live with you?"], [187.3, "They would not have been happy."], [189.6, "They would not have liked that."], [192.1, "They would think there's something wrong with me."], [194.9, "I can't support myself."], [196.6, "I can't get my own job."], [198.2, "I'm not independent."], [199.2, "That's not good."], [201.5, "So, and for me, I wouldn't like it because I don't want to live with my parents and I'm an adult."], [206.8, "I don't want them telling me what to do or anything like that."], [210.4, "So it's on both sides: both the children and the parents have this idea that when you're an adult, you leave home, and you should be independent and make your own decisions."], [223.9, "But I've met students from other countries who say it's very normal to live with their families until they're married."], [230.9, "And in some cultures, even after they get married, the couple will go and live with one of the families, the husband's family or the wife's family, and that's considered normal."], [241.7, "So in these cultures, family and the family's opinion continues to be important even when they're adults."], [248.6, "So maybe some of you listen to this article and you think, oh, this sounds normal."], [254.6, "Maybe some of you think this woman needs to worry about her family."], [258.2, "If her family doesn't like the situation maybe she should not date Will."], [263.4, "That might be a reaction that some people have."], [268.8, "However, Abby's answer is probably the normal answer most Americans would give, which is: stop worrying about your family's opinion."], [276.6, "Don't be a people pleaser, do what you want."], [280.2, "All right, next, the issue of double standards."], [283.8, "This was the second topic we discussed in my San Francisco class."], [288.5, "And the double standards refers to men and women."], [291.9, "And the fact that there are double standards for men and women when dating."], [297.2, "If a man dates a lot of women, it's often no problem."], [301.7, "People don't criticize him."], [303.4, "In fact, sometimes they think, hey, he's a cool guy."], [306.8, "Look at all those girlfriends he has."], [308.8, "This is great."], [309.8, "What a good guy."], [312.0, "And in some cultures, this double standard is very strong."], [316.2, "Right?"], [316.6, "Men can date a lot of women and people think it's good."], [320.4, "On the other hand, if a woman dates a lot of men."], [323.7, "Then she's bad, she's a bad girl, and people criticize her and people don't like it."], [331.5, "And that's clearly a double standard, right?"], [334.9, "That's the definition of double standard."], [337.8, "Two different rules for the same situation."], [341.3, "If a man does something, it's okay."], [343.5, "If a woman does it, it's not okay."], [345.4, "And in my class, there were clear double standards for most cultures."], [352.4, "Stronger in some countries, weaker in other countries."], [355.5, "This double standard does exist in America."], [358.2, "There's still a double standard between men and women when dating."], [362.0, "However, that double standard is getting weaker and weaker."], [366.3, "Women are getting more and more equal."], [369.3, "It's very normal now for a woman to date lots of different guys."], [373.5, "And it's generally not a problem."], [376.5, "This woman is in her 50s."], [377.8, "She's an older woman from an older generation."], [380.5, "Maybe that's why in this letter she sounds like she's a little bit criticizing her sister Jane for dating many men."], [388.0, "I think for younger Americans it's no problem."], [390.3, "It's just totally normal."], [392.4, "So this double standard is not so strong in America, getting weaker all the time."], [397.1, "In other countries in my class, some of the Asian students, for example, mentioned that this is a very strong double standard in their countries."], [407.0, "The men are almost encouraged to date a lot of girls, and it's seen as very cool."], [413.8, "But if a woman even has sex before she's married, something's wrong with her, she's a bad girl, everybody criticizes her."], [422.1, "And it's a strong double standard."], [424.5, "I guess the good news is most of them did mention that it's improving in all the countries in my class that were represented."], [434.1, "The students did say it's getting better."], [436.3, "Maybe it's still bad, but the double standards are improving in most places in the world."], [442.0, "And that's good."], [444.3, "Well, okay, those are our topics."], [446.1, "That's our commentary for this letter."], [448.3, "Hope you enjoyed it."], [449.6, "See you for the next lesson."], [451.5, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["double standard", "/ˌdʌbl ˈstændəd/", "tiêu chuẩn kép"], ["uneasy", "/ʌnˈiːzi/", "không yên lòng, bứt rứt"], ["ex-lover", "/ˌeks ˈlʌvə/", "người tình cũ"], ["mid-50s", "/ˌmɪd ˈfɪftiz/", "khoảng giữa tuổi 50"], ["numerous", "/ˈnjuːmərəs/", "rất nhiều"], ["affair", "/əˈfeə/", "cuộc tình, chuyện ngoại tình"], ["intimate", "/ˈɪntɪmət/", "thân mật, gần gũi"], ["terrific", "/təˈrɪfɪk/", "tuyệt vời"], ["break up with", "/breɪk ʌp wɪð/", "chia tay với"], ["presently", "/ˈprezntli/", "hiện giờ"], ["engaged", "/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒd/", "đã đính hôn"], ["become involved", "/bɪˈkʌm ɪnˈvɒlvd/", "bắt đầu quan hệ, dính líu"], ["see each other", "/siː iːtʃ ˈʌðə/", "hẹn hò với nhau"], ["fall in love", "/fɔːl ɪn lʌv/", "phải lòng, yêu"], ["betray", "/bɪˈtreɪ/", "phản bội"], ["former", "/ˈfɔːmə/", "cũ, trước đây"], ["current", "/ˈkʌrənt/", "hiện tại"], ["family gathering", "/ˈfæməli ˈɡæðərɪŋ/", "buổi họp mặt gia đình"], ["concerned", "/kənˈsɜːnd/", "lo ngại"], ["weird", "/wɪəd/", "kỳ quặc"], ["bow to pressure", "/baʊ tə ˈpreʃə/", "khuất phục trước áp lực"], ["give up", "/ɡɪv ʌp/", "từ bỏ"], ["approve of", "/əˈpruːv ɒv/", "tán thành, chấp thuận"], ["won't budge", "/wəʊnt bʌdʒ/", "không chịu nhượng bộ"], ["confront", "/kənˈfrʌnt/", "đối mặt"], ["sophisticated", "/səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd/", "sành sỏi, từng trải"], ["serial", "/ˈsɪəriəl/", "liên tiếp, hết cái này đến cái khác"], ["worldly", "/ˈwɜːldli/", "từng trải"], ["turn a blind eye to", "/tɜːn ə blaɪnd aɪ tuː/", "làm ngơ trước"], ["be entitled to", "/bi ɪnˈtaɪtld tuː/", "có quyền được"], ["awkward", "/ˈɔːkwəd/", "ngượng ngùng"], ["grown-up", "/ˈɡrəʊn ʌp/", "người lớn"], ["get past", "/ɡet pɑːst/", "vượt qua"], ["people pleaser", "/ˈpiːpl ˈpliːzə/", "người luôn chiều lòng người khác"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["Family is uneasy", "Gia đình không yên lòng"], ["in our mid-50s", "khoảng 55 tuổi"], ["over the past several years", "trong mấy năm qua"], ["was involved in an intimate relationship with", "từng có quan hệ thân mật với"], ["he wasn't what she was looking for", "anh ấy không phải người cô ấy tìm kiếm"], ["engaged to be married", "đã đính hôn"], ["we started seeing each other again", "chúng tôi bắt đầu hẹn hò lại"], ["we have fallen in love", "chúng tôi đã yêu nhau"], ["says I have betrayed her", "nói rằng tôi đã phản bội cô ấy"], ["it's just weird", "chuyện đó thật kỳ quặc"], ["it sure bothers them", "chắc chắn làm họ bận tâm"], ["bowed to their pressure", "khuất phục trước áp lực của họ"], ["more than I could have ever imagined", "hơn cả những gì tôi từng tưởng tượng"], ["give up my future happiness", "từ bỏ hạnh phúc tương lai"], ["won't budge", "không chịu nhượng bộ"], ["Any suggestions?", "Có lời khuyên nào không?"], ["stop being the good girl", "thôi làm đứa con ngoan"], ["a woman who knows what she wants", "người phụ nữ biết mình muốn gì"], ["confront the double standard", "đối mặt với tiêu chuẩn kép"], ["turned a blind eye to it", "làm ngơ chuyện đó"], ["you are entitled to your happiness too", "bạn cũng có quyền được hạnh phúc"], ["everyone should be able to get past it", "ai cũng nên vượt qua được"], ["a people pleaser for the rest of your life", "người chiều lòng thiên hạ suốt đời"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["S + be + uneasy + about / when + clause", "I feel uneasy when he drives fast.", "Tôi thấy bất an khi anh ấy lái xe nhanh.", "uneasy"], ["S + be + in + one's + early/mid/late + 20s/30s...", "My parents are in their late 60s.", "Bố mẹ tôi gần 70 tuổi.", "in their|in our|in his|in her|in my"], ["S + be + not + what + S + be + looking for", "This job is not what I'm looking for.", "Công việc này không phải thứ tôi đang tìm.", "looking for"], ["S + be + engaged to (be married to) + someone", "My sister is engaged to a doctor.", "Chị tôi đã đính hôn với một bác sĩ.", "engaged"], ["S + start(ed) + seeing + someone", "She started seeing a new guy last month.", "Cô ấy bắt đầu hẹn hò với một anh chàng mới từ tháng trước.", "seeing"], ["The fact that + clause + V ...", "The fact that he lied bothers me.", "Việc anh ấy nói dối làm tôi bận tâm.", "the fact that"], ["S + bow(ed) to + (one's) pressure", "The company didn't bow to their pressure.", "Công ty không khuất phục trước áp lực của họ.", "bow to|bowed to|bow to the"], ["... more than I could have ever imagined", "This trip was better than I could have ever imagined.", "Chuyến đi này tuyệt hơn tôi từng tưởng tượng.", "could have ever imagined|could have imagined"], ["S + won't budge (on + something)", "My boss won't budge on the deadline.", "Sếp tôi không chịu lùi hạn chót.", "won't budge|wouldn't budge"], ["Perhaps it's time to + V", "Perhaps it's time to look for a new job.", "Có lẽ đã đến lúc tìm việc mới.", "time to"], ["S + turn(ed) a blind eye to + something", "The teacher turned a blind eye to the noise.", "Cô giáo làm ngơ trước tiếng ồn.", "blind eye"], ["S + be + entitled to + noun", "Every worker is entitled to a holiday.", "Mọi người lao động đều có quyền được nghỉ phép.", "entitled to"], ["S + should be able to + get past + something", "You should be able to get past this problem.", "Bạn nên vượt qua được vấn đề này.", "get past"], ["S + have to decide whether + to V / clause", "I have to decide whether to stay or leave.", "Tôi phải quyết định nên ở lại hay ra đi.", "decide whether"]]$j$::jsonb
