ll, it's him saying, all Buddhists serve the devil."], [567.1, "s", "That's the final bad thing that makes me lose control, lose my temper."], [574.1, "s", "So he says, all Buddhists serve the devil."], [576.9, "s", "That's the straw that breaks the camel's back."], [580.6, "s", "When he asks me, are your relatives also Buddhist?"], [585.3, "s", "Is that the last straw?"], [586.8, "q", "Is that the straw that breaks the camel's back?"], [592.0, "a", "No, no."], [593.0, "s", "I'm patient after he says that it's no problem."], [596.8, "q", "Okay, so what is the straw that breaks the camel's back?"], [602.6, "a", "Well, it's when he says all Buddhists serve the devil."], [605.7, "s", "That's the straw that breaks the camel's back."], [608.0, "s", "It's the final insult, then I get angry and I yell at him, go away!"], [612.3, "s", "I refuse to listen to you anymore."], [616.3, "q", "Will I listen to him again?"], [619.8, "a", "No."], [621.4, "s", "I refuse to listen to him anymore."], [624.7, "s", "I will never listen to him again."], [626.5, "s", "I refuse."], [627.2, "s", "I say no, I won't do it."], [629.2, "s", "No, I will never listen to you again."], [632.7, "s", "I refuse to listen to him anymore."], [636.4, "q", "Do I refuse to listen to all Christians?"], [641.6, "a", "No, no."], [642.9, "s", "I don't mind all Christians."], [644.6, "s", "It's just this one guy."], [646.1, "s", "I refuse to listen to him ever again."], [649.3, "s", "I will never listen to him again."], [651.9, "s", "I refuse to listen to him, only to him."], [654.9, "s", "I refuse to listen to him."], [658.5, "q", "Do I refuse to watch television again?"], [662.6, "a", "No, I don't refuse to watch television."], [665.7, "q", "What do I refuse to do?"], [669.8, "a", "Well, I refuse to listen to that guy again, right?"], [673.6, "s", "I refuse to listen to him again."], [677.3, "s", "All right."], [678.3, "s", "That's the end of our little story."], [680.5, "s", "One more time."], [682.2, "s", "This time with pauses after the key phrases."], [685.4, "s", "I'll pause."], [686.8, "s", "Say the key phrase after I pause."], [689.9, "s", "Copy my pronunciation."], [691.7, "s", "That's the important part of this section."], [694.9, "s", "Copy my pronunciation, especially my intonation."], [697.6, "s", "When I go up, when I go down, things like that."], [701.1, "s", "Okay."], [701.4, "s", "Let's go."], [702.3, "s", "I'm walking down the street when a guy comes to me and says,"], [705.7, "s", "“Hi, can I chat with you for a moment?”"], [708.2, "s", "He looks clean and very neat."], [710.5, "s", "I'm quite naive."], [713.8, "s", "I'm quite naive."], [717.5, "s", "I'm quite naive."], [720.0, "s", "So I think he's just friendly."], [722.3, "s", "I say, okay."], [724.2, "s", "The man asks me, how far would you go to save yourself?"], [731.8, "s", "How far would you go to save yourself?"], [738.6, "s", "How far would you go to save yourself?"], [744.1, "s", "Good."], [744.8, "s", "I say, what do you mean?"], [748.1, "s", "He says, I'm talking about the Christian faith."], [752.6, "s", "I'm talking about the Christian faith."], [758.9, "s", "I want you to convert to Christianity."], [765.1, "s", "I want you to convert to Christianity."], [770.1, "s", "Good."], [770.8, "s", "I say, actually, I'm a Buddhist."], [774.8, "s", "And he asks, what about your relatives?"], [779.5, "s", "Are they Buddhists too?"], [782.2, "s", "What about your relatives?"], [783.9, "s", "Are they Buddhists too?"], [788.3, "s", "What about your relatives?"], [790.0, "s", "Are they Buddhists too?"], [793.9, "s", "I tell him no, just me."], [796.7, "s", "He then tells me that I will go to hell if I don't convert."], [805.0, "s", "He then tells me that I will go to hell if I don't convert."], [813.8, "s", "He says I'm a bad person."], [815.7, "s", "He tells me all Buddhists will go to hell."], [818.9, "s", "Finally,"], [819.2, "s", "he says that the Buddha and all Buddhists serve the devil."], [823.9, "s", "That's the straw that breaks the camel's back."], [831.1, "s", "That's the straw that breaks the camel's back."], [839.2, "s", "That's the straw that breaks the camel's back."], [844.6, "s", "I yell at him, go away!"], [846.6, "s", "I refuse to listen to you anymore."], [853.0, "s", "I refuse to listen to you anymore."], [858.6, "s", "I refuse to listen to you anymore."], [861.9, "s", "Okay, great job."], [864.1, "s", "Now the final part of the mini story lesson."], [867.8, "s", "Pause your iPod, pause your computer, and try to tell all of the story yourself."], [875.2, "s", "Tell all of it out loud so you can hear it."], [878.7, "s", "Tell all of the story."], [880.2, "s", "You don't need to remember every word, but try to use the target vocabulary, the new vocabulary, correctly."], [888.9, "s", "If you can't, if you have trouble, no problem, relax, listen to it again."], [894.7, "s", "Just keep listening until you can pause and tell all of the story yourself."], [900.2, "s", "Okay, see you next time."], [901.4, "s", "Bye-bye."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.4, "Welcome to the Point of View mini-stories for Greek Family."], [4.9, "Let's get started."], [5.0, "First, the past tense."], [6.5, "Five years ago, I was walking down the street when a guy came to me and said, “Hi, can I chat with you for a moment?”"], [14.2, "He looked clean and very neat."], [16.0, "I was quite naive, so I thought he was just being friendly."], [20.5, "I said, okay."], [22.2, "The man asked me, how far would you go to save yourself?"], [26.4, "I said, what do you mean?"], [28.9, "He said, I'm talking about the Christian faith."], [32.7, "I want you to convert to Christianity."], [34.8, "“Actually, I'm a Buddhist,” I said."], [37.3, "“What about your relatives?"], [38.4, "Are they Buddhists too?” he asked."], [41.0, "I told him no, just me."], [44.2, "He then told me that I would go to hell if I didn't convert."], [48.2, "He said I was a bad person."], [50.2, "He told me all Buddhists would go to hell."], [52.6, "Finally, he said that the Buddha and all Buddhists served the devil."], [56.7, "That was the last straw."], [58.1, "It was the straw that broke the camel's back."], [61.4, "I yelled at him."], [62.4, "“Go away!"], [63.6, "I refuse to listen to you anymore!”"], [67.6, "All right, our second version."], [70.4, "I'm gonna change this a little bit, so you get a little more practice."], [75.9, "Just change the order of the story."], [78.6, "Since I was a child, I have been very naive."], [84.5, "I have always thought that people are very friendly, even if they're not."], [91.0, "I have always accepted people and not worried about them or been suspicious."], [97.5, "Right?"], [97.8, "I've always been quite naive since I was a child."], [101.8, "Well, one day I was walking down the street when a guy came up to me and said,"], [106.7, "“Hi."], [107.2, "Can I chat with you for a moment?”"], [109.0, "He looked clean and very neat."], [112.1, "Since I was quite naive and have always been naive, I thought he was just being friendly."], [117.5, "So I said, okay."], [118.8, "The man asked me, how far would you go to save yourself?"], [123.1, "I said, what do you mean?"], [125.3, "He said, I'm talking about the Christian faith."], [128.2, "I want you to convert to Christianity."], [130.8, "“Actually, I'm a Buddhist,” I said."], [132.9, "“What about your relatives?"], [134.4, "Are they Buddhists too?” he asked."], [136.6, "I told him no, just me."], [138.7, "He then told me that I would go to hell if I didn't convert."], [143.8, "He said I was a bad person."], [146.3, "He told me all Buddhists would go to hell."], [149.6, "Finally he said that the Buddha and all Buddhists served the devil."], [153.9, "That was the last straw."], [155.6, "That was the straw that broke the camel's back."], [158.5, "I yelled at him, go away!"], [160.2, "I refuse to listen to you anymore."], [164.9, "So you can notice I use the present perfect, “have been”, for something that started long ago, when I was a child, and continued up to the time this story happened."], [177.8, "Then I changed to the simple past, because we're talking about one specific event, and it's already happened, it's done."], [186.9, "Okay, now let's go to the future."], [189.7, "Back to the future."], [190.6, "Here we go."], [191.5, "In 10 years, 10 years from now, I'm imagining this."], [196.2, "Maybe I dreamed this."], [198.0, "Okay."], [198.1, "This is a dream."], [199.0, "I have a dream in 10 years."], [201.2, "I will be walking down the street when a guy will come up to me and he'll say,"], [206.2, "“Hi, can I chat with you for a moment?”"], [209.3, "He'll look clean and very neat."], [211.6, "I'll be quite naive, so I'll think he's just being friendly."], [215.3, "I'll say, okay."], [216.7, "The man's gonna ask me, how far would you go to save yourself?"], [222.6, "And I'll say, what do you mean?"], [225.3, "He'll say, I'm talking about the Christian faith, I want you to convert to Christianity."], [231.8, "“Actually, I'm a Buddhist,” I'll say."], [233.5, "Okay?"], [234.2, "“What about your relatives?"], [235.9, "Are they Buddhists too?” he'll ask."], [238.9, "I'm gonna tell him, no, just me."], [242.9, "He'll then tell me that I will go to hell if I don't convert."], [246.6, "He'll say I'm a bad person."], [248.5, "He'll tell me all Buddhists will go to hell."], [250.8, "Finally, he'll say that the Buddha and all Buddhists serve the devil."], [255.1, "That's gonna be the straw that breaks the camel's back."], [258.4, "I'll yell at him, go away."], [260.8, "I refuse to listen to you anymore."], [265.8, "All right."], [266.3, "Go back."], [267.6, "Listen to each version."], [270.0, "After each version, pause and try to tell that version yourself out loud so you can hear it."], [277.6, "So listen to the first version, the past."], [280.4, "Pause and tell the whole story again using the past: five years ago."], [285.7, "Second time."], [286.9, "Start the story with, you know, “since I was a child”, and tell the story yourself out loud."], [288.0, "And then again, listen to the future version, and pause and tell the future version yourself."], [288.9, "If it's difficult, if you can't do it, no problem."], [289.5, "Just relax, go back, listen very carefully again and again and again, and then try again."], [290.4, "All right, I'll see you next time."], [290.8, "Bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.5, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for Greek Family."], [8.0, "So this is another one of those interesting Dear Abby letters."], [12.3, "Again, quite short, but it has some good little phrases and words, like “naive”, “broke the camel's back” or “the straw that broke the camel's back”."], [24.7, "But the basic topic here is really intercultural dating, or marriage, or relationships, right?"], [31.9, "Having a relationship with somebody from another culture."], [36.7, "Maybe you guys have seen the movie My Big Fat Greek Wedding."], [41.5, "In fact, it's a good movie, it's funny, and it's about this topic."], [46.4, "This man dates a woman who has a Greek family, and the Greek family doesn't like him because he's not Greek."], [54.9, "Right?"], [55.3, "They have a very strong idea that she should only date other Greek people."], [60.5, "So there's a big problem with her family."], [63.4, "It's a comedy, so it's not too serious, but it's the same basic idea."], [68.5, "So, you know, maybe some of you... I don't know, what do you think about this idea of dating people or having relationships with people from other cultures?"], [78.8, "Now, certainly Tomoe and I have this issue."], [81.8, "She's sitting right here on the bed right now."], [85.1, "And we sometimes have difficulties because of our different cultures and languages."], [94.2, "We have a language barrier."], [96.6, "We communicate with each other in English because I know very, very, very little Japanese."], [105.4, "And her English is good, so that's how we communicate."], [110.8, "But it's not her native language."], [112.1, "So sometimes she says something and she means something, and I hear something else."], [118.9, "something she doesn't mean, and we have a miscommunication, and that can cause problems sometimes."], [125.1, "Sometimes we have big arguments, but really it's just a misunderstanding, a language misunderstanding."], [132.3, "Sometimes it might be a culture misunderstanding."], [135.3, "Of course Japanese culture and American culture are different."], [140.6, "We all know, you know, some of the stereotypes, but, you know, there are little things and sometimes big things that are different."], [149.9, "And it can be hard for us to understand each other about those points."], [155.5, "So it's a little bit of extra difficulty when you date someone from another culture."], [163.7, "And especially if different languages are involved."], [166.8, "Now, on the other hand, it's also an opportunity to learn and grow, right?"], [173.1, "You learn about a lot of new things."], [176.1, "The other person has different ideas."], [179.4, "Different views."], [181.2, "Different points of view on life from your own and from your own culture, and that can help you grow and learn more about the world, and hopefully be more open and flexible."], [194.5, "And that's great."], [196.1, "In fact, that's one of the benefits also of just traveling in general or learning another language."], [202.2, "You go beyond your own little small country and most of us, we grow up and we're told that our country is the best, right?"], [211.8, "And we know this is true when we're young."], [214.6, "All Americans know that America is number one."], [218.1, "America is the best country in the world."], [221.1, "In fact, a lot of Americans believe that even adults."], [225.0, "I'd say probably most Americans believe that they think everything in America is the best and other countries are not as good."], [234.3, "We're the best at everything."], [236.8, "Everything we do is good and correct."], [240.3, "And you know, people get mad at the United States because of this."], [246.8, "Mainly because the United States has a lot of power right now and we don't use that power very well."], [254.2, "However, I've traveled to many countries, and I can tell you that most Japanese people think Japan is number one, and it's the best culture and country in the world."], [263.6, "And most Thai people think that Thailand is the best country in the world."], [268.0, "Now, they know it's not the richest, but they still think, you know, our culture, it's still the best."], [274.0, "And I think most people think that."], [276.2, "Most people are taught that when they grow up."], [279.1, "They're taught by their parents."], [280.7, "They're taught by their society."], [283.0, "By their media, that there's something special about their country which is better than others."], [289.1, "And while it's nice to like your country, it's a dangerous idea."], [295.5, "Travel can help to get rid of that illusion."], [303.2, "And an illusion is something that's not true, but you believe it is true."], [308.4, "Of course, I never really thought America was always number one, but, you know, I didn't understand the rest of the world."], [313.4, "When I traveled to India, the first time I left America, I saw, wow, you know,"], [319.1, "there are other ways of living."], [321.2, "There are other ways of doing things."], [323.7, "And some of them are better than America."], [326.0, "Some of them I liked better."], [327.7, "There were many parts of Indian culture, and parts of the country in general, that I thought were better than the United States."], [336.3, "And there were other parts where I thought America was quite good."], [340.8, "And then later I traveled to Japan and lived there, and Korea and lived there, and Thailand and lived there."], [348.3, "And I traveled in Italy a little bit and in England a little bit."], [353.6, "And I started to realize, wow, there are many ways of living, many ways to do things, many different religions, many things to believe."], [362.6, "And you know, there is no best country."], [365.6, "Certainly America's not the best, but none of these countries were the best."], [370.5, "They all had great things."], [372.4, "They all had very nice things about them that were different and unique and special."], [378.0, "And so that's a great thing about travel, and a great thing about learning a language, and a great thing about connecting with people from other countries."], [388.1, "And it can also be a great thing about dating people or having a relationship with someone from another country, because then it becomes very personal."], [397.9, "When you travel, it's not so personal."], [400.5, "You go to a country and you see it and you learn something, and then you go home."], [407.3, "If you live there for a while, it's a little deeper, of course."], [412.2, "But if you have a relationship with someone from another country, it's even more deep, because then you really start to see how differently people think and how different people's beliefs can be."], [424.5, "And you know, that can be very good."], [427.5, "It's sometimes difficult, but in general I think it's very good."], [431.7, "It certainly has been very good for me and has helped me open my mind more to the world."], [438.8, "And hopefully not be a typical American."], [445.0, "Another issue: in the mini-story, I told a little mini-story about somebody on the street"], [452.0, "coming up to me and trying to make me become a Christian, and actually this is kind of a true story."], [458.0, "It's based on a true story because I used to live in Georgia and also South Carolina in the United States."], [466.1, "These areas are in the southeast part of America, and the southeast is very, very Christian."], [473.2, "When I say Christian, I mean Protestant, Baptist mostly, and very evangelical."], [480.2, "Evangelical means they're aggressive."], [483.3, "They try to change people's religion."], [486.7, "And so I would be walking around my town, and this would happen."], [491.1, "This happened to me especially in South Carolina."], [494.5, "People would walk up to me and start talking to me, and then very soon they would start talking about religion."], [501.8, "And they would criticize me and attack me because I wasn't part of their religion."], [507.0, "And you know, I really actually hate that about southern culture in the southeast part of the United States."], [513.7, "I like some things about the South, but I really hated that part, because I was often bothered by these people, and it's a kind of intolerance."], [524.8, "It's a kind of what I was just talking about with travel."], [529.1, "These people usually had never been outside of America."], [535.0, "They had no contact, no experience with people of other religions."], [542.0, "They criticized Islam, for example, but they had never met a Muslim person."], [547.5, "They certainly had never read the Quran."], [550.5, "Until they met me, they had never met a Buddhist before, and I'm only kind of a cowboy American Buddhist."], [557.6, "I don't know if that's real or not."], [561.1, "So they really have no experience of the world."], [564.4, "And so if you have no experience of the world, you're quite naive."], [569.1, "And when you're naive, it's easy to have very strong beliefs about something,"], [573.9, "about a religion or about something else."], [576.2, "It's easy to believe you're the best and you're always right if you never have experiences of other people in other places that have different beliefs that are also quite good or quite interesting or quite powerful or quite helpful."], [590.8, "And you know, South Carolina is a small little place."], [593.3, "Most people in South Carolina have never traveled outside the United States, many have never traveled outside of South Carolina."], [601.9, "They've never been to a big American city, even."], [605.6, "So their experience is very small."], [608.2, "It's quite naive."], [610.2, "And so living there was a bit difficult."], [612.6, "It wasn't only these kind of Christian people."], [617.5, "It was many other kinds of things."], [621.4, "They had these very narrow, small beliefs."], [625.2, "And they wouldn't debate them, they wouldn't consider other ideas."], [629.5, "It was just, they're right, and you're wrong."], [633.2, "And unfortunately, we see that in the United States, in our government right now, this same mentality."], [640.5, "I would say George Bush has this mentality, and the people who support George Bush have this mentality."], [646.3, "George Bush is very popular in South Carolina, for example, still very popular."], [651.5, "In the rest of the country, not so popular, but in places like South Carolina, he's still very popular."], [659.1, "And he has the same kind of mentality: America's number one, everything we do is the best, Islamic people, Muslim people are totally wrong and bad, any other part of the world, they're not as good as we are."], [674.8, "These are beliefs that are common in parts of America,"], [678.8, "and unfortunately common in our government right now."], [683.5, "So I don't know if we can make more Americans travel or meet people from other countries."], [688.6, "Maybe that might help."], [689.8, "I don't know."], [690.9, "That's your job."], [692.1, "Meet some Americans and teach them about the world."], [694.4, "Teach them about your country."], [696.8, "All right, well, I guess that's all for the commentary."], [699.1, "I guess I talked about several topics this time."], [702.7, "I hope you're enjoying Effortless English, and look at the forums."], [706.4, "I need your help."], [707.4, "I've put a couple forum ideas asking for your help and your contribution, your actions."], [715.9, "So go read the forums and help improve the Effortless English Club."], [719.8, "See you next time."], [720.9, "Bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["Greek", "/ɡriːk/", "người Hy Lạp; thuộc Hy Lạp"], ["accept", "/əkˈsept/", "chấp nhận"], ["naive", "/naɪˈiːv/", "ngây thơ, cả tin"], ["fit in", "/fɪt ɪn/", "hòa nhập"], ["convert", "/kənˈvɜːt/", "cải đạo, chuyển đổi"], ["Catholicism", "/kəˈθɒləsɪzəm/", "Công giáo"], ["Orthodox", "/ˈɔːθədɒks/", "Chính thống giáo"], ["faith", "/feɪθ/", "đức tin, tôn giáo"], ["attend", "/əˈtend/", "tham dự"], ["family function", "/ˈfæməli ˈfʌŋkʃn/", "buổi tiệc, sự kiện gia đình"], ["relatives", "/ˈrelətɪvz/", "họ hàng"], ["extended family", "/ɪkˈstendɪd ˈfæməli/", "đại gia đình, họ hàng xa"], ["refuse", "/rɪˈfjuːz/", "từ chối"], ["share", "/ʃeə/", "dùng chung, chia sẻ"], ["priest", "/priːst/", "linh mục"], ["the straw that broke the camel's back", "/ðə strɔː ðət brəʊk ðə ˈkæməlz bæk/", "giọt nước tràn ly"], ["father-in-law", "/ˈfɑːðər ɪn lɔː/", "bố chồng, bố vợ"], ["grandchildren", "/ˈɡræntʃɪldrən/", "các cháu"], ["heritage", "/ˈherɪtɪdʒ/", "dòng dõi, di sản"], ["receive", "/rɪˈsiːv/", "nhận"], ["neutral", "/ˈnjuːtrəl/", "trung lập"], ["how far", "/haʊ fɑː/", "đến mức nào"], ["chat", "/tʃæt/", "trò chuyện"], ["neat", "/niːt/", "gọn gàng, chỉn chu"], ["Christianity", "/ˌkrɪstiˈænəti/", "Cơ Đốc giáo"], ["Buddhist", "/ˈbʊdɪst/", "Phật tử"], ["hell", "/hel/", "địa ngục"], ["serve the devil", "/sɜːv ðə ˈdevl/", "phục vụ quỷ dữ"], ["the last straw", "/ðə lɑːst strɔː/", "giọt nước tràn ly"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["whose family never accepted me", "gia đình anh ấy chưa bao giờ chấp nhận tôi"], ["being young and naive", "vì còn trẻ và ngây thơ"], ["I tried everything to fit in", "tôi đã thử mọi cách để hòa nhập"], ["converting from Catholicism to the Greek Orthodox faith", "cải đạo từ Công giáo sang Chính thống giáo Hy Lạp"], ["attending all family functions", "dự mọi buổi tiệc gia đình"], ["It was never enough.", "Chừng đó chưa bao giờ là đủ."], ["visit his relatives there", "thăm họ hàng của anh ấy ở đó"], ["refused to share the dinner table with me", "từ chối ngồi chung bàn ăn với tôi"], ["was born four years later", "ra đời bốn năm sau đó"], ["what broke the camel's back for me", "giọt nước tràn ly đối với tôi"], ["of Greek heritage", "có dòng máu Hy Lạp"], ["cried for hours", "khóc hàng giờ liền"], ["tried to stay neutral", "cố giữ thái độ trung lập"], ["how far should someone have to go", "một người phải cố đến mức nào"], ["fit in with their husband's family", "hòa nhập với gia đình chồng"], ["Can I chat with you for a moment?", "Tôi nói chuyện với bạn một chút được không?"], ["How far would you go to save yourself?", "Bạn sẵn sàng làm đến mức nào để cứu lấy bản thân?"], ["I refuse to listen to you anymore.", "Tôi không thèm nghe anh nói nữa."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["S + married + someone + whose + noun + V", "I married a man whose parents live in Hue.", "Tôi lấy một người đàn ông có bố mẹ sống ở Huế.", "whose"], ["Being + adj, S + V ...", "Being tired, I went to bed early.", "Vì mệt nên tôi đi ngủ sớm.", "being"], ["S + tried everything to + V", "I tried everything to lose weight.", "Tôi đã thử mọi cách để giảm cân.", "tried everything|try everything"], ["S + fit(s) in (with + someone)", "It's hard to fit in at a new school.", "Thật khó để hòa nhập ở trường mới.", "fit in"], ["S + convert(ed) from A to B", "He converted from Buddhism to Christianity.", "Anh ấy cải đạo từ Phật giáo sang Cơ Đốc giáo.", "convert|converted"], ["It was never enough.", "I worked hard, but it was never enough.", "Tôi làm việc chăm chỉ, nhưng chừng đó chưa bao giờ là đủ.", "never enough"], ["S + refused to + V", "She refused to answer my question.", "Cô ấy từ chối trả lời câu hỏi của tôi.", "refused to|refuse to"], ["What broke the camel's back (for me) was + noun", "What broke the camel's back for me was his lie.", "Giọt nước tràn ly đối với tôi là lời nói dối của anh ta.", "camel's back"], ["That's the straw that breaks the camel's back.", "He was late again. That's the straw that breaks the camel's back.", "Anh ta lại đến muộn. Đó là giọt nước tràn ly.", "straw|last straw"], ["S + cried / waited / talked + for hours", "We talked for hours last night.", "Tối qua chúng tôi nói chuyện hàng giờ liền.", "for hours"], ["S + tried to stay + adj", "I tried to stay calm.", "Tôi đã cố giữ bình tĩnh.", "stay"], ["How far would you go to + V?", "How far would you go to win?", "Bạn sẵn sàng làm đến mức nào để chiến thắng?", "how far"], ["Can I + V + with you for a moment?", "Can I talk with you for a moment?", "Tôi nói chuyện với bạn một chút được không?", "for a moment"], ["I refuse to + V + anymore.", "I refuse to wait anymore.", "Tôi không chịu chờ thêm nữa.", "refuse to|anymore"]]$j$::jsonb
