ks free, he jumps up and kicks the man in the head."], [655.0, "s", "Boom!"], [656.8, "s", "The man falls down unconscious."], [660.9, "s", "Jim wins the fight, and he yells, no matter how you slice it, I just kicked your ass."], [670.5, "s", "Alright, no matter how you slice it means no matter what your opinion."], [676.4, "s", "No matter how you look at it."], [679.0, "s", "Any angle."], [680.3, "s", "Any way you look at it, any opinion."], [683.2, "s", "Everybody will agree Jim kicked his ass."], [688.0, "s", "And of course, kicked your ass means to beat somebody, to win against them."], [693.3, "q", "Okay, so no matter how you slice it, did Jim lose?"], [698.5, "a", "No matter how you slice it, any opinion will agree, Jim won the fight."], [706.4, "q", "No matter how you slice it, is George Bush an idiot?"], [711.4, "a", "Yes, that's right, everybody agrees that George Bush is an idiot."], [715.2, "s", "No matter how you slice it, any way you look at it, any opinion, everybody agrees George Bush is an idiot."], [722.4, "q", "No matter how you slice it, is Jim a strong man?"], [727.7, "a", "Yeah, that's right."], [728.7, "s", "I think so."], [729.6, "s", "No matter how you slice it, Jim is a strong guy."], [732.2, "s", "He's a tough guy."], [733.2, "s", "Everybody agrees now."], [734.9, "s", "No matter how you slice it, Jim is a strong guy."], [739.8, "q", "Did Jim kick the man's ass?"], [744.3, "a", "Yes, he did."], [745.1, "s", "Jim kicked his ass."], [746.8, "q", "Whose ass did Jim kick?"], [751.1, "a", "Well, Jim kicked the big man's ass."], [753.9, "s", "The big man from the gym, right?"], [755.9, "s", "He kicked his ass."], [758.3, "q", "Does everybody agree that Jim kicked his ass?"], [764.0, "a", "Yeah, everybody agrees."], [765.2, "s", "No matter how you slice it, Jim won the fight."], [768.8, "s", "Jim kicked his ass."], [771.4, "s", "All right, very good."], [773.6, "s", "Let's go on back to the top again."], [775.5, "s", "This time, I will pause after the key words or phrases, please copy my pronunciation."], [782.2, "s", "This is not a grammar exercise."], [784.6, "s", "This is a pronunciation exercise, so please focus on pronunciation."], [790.1, "s", "Here we go."], [791.7, "s", "There's a very small man named Jim."], [794.0, "s", "Jim is only one foot tall."], [797.0, "s", "Even though Jim is 48 years old, people always perceive him as a child."], [805.5, "s", "People always perceive him as a child."], [808.4, "s", "In the eyes of the public, Jim is just a cute little boy."], [821.4, "s", "In the eyes of the public, Jim is just a cute little boy."], [829.8, "s", "Jim hates this."], [831.2, "s", "He says, I want people to accept me as I really am."], [835.7, "s", "I want them to give me unconditional respect."], [843.2, "s", "I want them to give me unconditional respect."], [846.7, "s", "He says, I don't want people to go on treating me like a child."], [859.4, "s", "I don't want people to go on treating me like a child."], [867.1, "s", "So Jim goes to the gym and exercises every day."], [871.3, "s", "He becomes very strong."], [873.9, "s", "He also learns kickboxing."], [876.0, "s", "One day a tall big man sees him and laughs and says, you're such a cute little man."], [883.6, "s", "Jim gets angry."], [884.9, "s", "He yells and says, I'm going to kick your ass."], [889.2, "s", "He kicks the man."], [890.7, "s", "They start fighting."], [892.7, "s", "The fight lasts for 20 hours."], [897.9, "s", "The fight lasts for 20 hours."], [902.9, "s", "The men's hands and legs become intertwined."], [910.1, "s", "The men's hands and legs become intertwined."], [917.0, "s", "They fall down."], [918.8, "s", "Jim finally breaks away from the man."], [924.2, "s", "Jim finally breaks away from the man."], [926.2, "s", "Then he jumps up and kicks the man in the head."], [932.4, "s", "Jim wins the fight and he yells, no matter how you slice it, I just kicked your ass."], [941.7, "s", "No matter how you slice it, I just kicked your ass."], [947.3, "s", "Alright very good."], [948.5, "s", "Please pause now."], [949.7, "s", "Try to tell all of the story yourself."], [952.4, "s", "Tell everything yourself."], [953.9, "s", "If you can't remember, relax, go back, listen again."], [958.1, "s", "Alright, now for the POV point of view stories, next!"]]}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.0, "Okay, welcome to the POV mini-stories,"], [3.9, "point of view mini-stories,"], [5.9, "for the Longtime Affair lesson."], [8.8, "Same story, different versions."], [11.0, "Let's start."], [12.5, "First, we go to the past."], [15.3, "Ten years ago."], [16.9, "Ten years ago, there was a very small man named Jim."], [21.8, "Jim was only one foot tall."], [23.9, "Even though Jim was 48 years old, people always perceived him as a child."], [31.1, "In the eyes of the public, Jim was just a cute little boy."], [35.6, "Jim hated this."], [36.9, "He said, I want people to accept me as I really am."], [40.9, "I want them to give me unconditional respect."], [44.6, "I don't want people to go on treating me like a child."], [48.9, "So, Jim went to the gym and exercised every day."], [52.7, "He became very strong."], [55.4, "He also learned kickboxing."], [57.6, "One day, a tall man saw him, laughed, and said, You're such a cute little man."], [65.7, "Jim got angry."], [67.1, "He yelled and said, I'm gonna kick your ass."], [72.0, "He kicked the man."], [73.4, "They started to fight."], [75.1, "The fight lasted for 20 hours."], [77.2, "The men's hands and legs became intertwined and they fell down."], [83.8, "Jim finally broke free from the man."], [86.3, "Then he jumped up and kicked the man in the head."], [89.9, "Jim won the fight and he yelled, no matter how you slice it, I just kicked your ass."], [97.6, "All right, that's our past version."], [100.2, "Now let's move to the perfect version, we call it, I guess."], [104.3, "Here we go."], [107.2, "Since last year."], [111.4, "Since last year."], [116.5, "There's a very small man named Jim."], [118.9, "Jim is only one foot tall."], [122.4, "Even though Jim is 48 years old, people have always perceived him as a child."], [129.1, "In the eyes of the public, Jim has always been just a cute little boy."], [135.8, "Jim has always hated this, but since last year, he has become very upset."], [144.2, "Every day he has said, I want people to accept me as I really am."], [149.7, "I want them to give me unconditional respect."], [153.0, "I don't want people to go on treating me as a child."], [157.5, "And so, since last year, Jim has gone to the gym and has exercised every day."], [163.9, "He has become very strong."], [166.9, "He has also learned kickboxing."], [170.5, "Well, one day a tall, big man saw him and laughed and said, you're such a cute little man."], [177.4, "Jim got angry."], [178.7, "He yelled and he kicked the man."], [181.2, "They started to fight."], [182.8, "The fight lasted for 20 hours."], [185.0, "The men's hands and legs became intertwined and they fell down."], [190.5, "Jim finally broke away from the man."], [192.7, "Then he jumped up and kicked him in the head."], [195.6, "Jim won the fight and he yelled, no matter how you slice it, I just kicked your ass."], [204.3, "All right."], [204.8, "In that version, you notice that we use, we call it, the present perfect."], [210.1, "It doesn't matter."], [210.7, "You don't need to know the name of the grammar, but we use that form, “have gone”, “have been”, because it's something that has continued through the past for a while: started in the past, kept going for a while."], [224.4, "For example, people have always perceived him as a child."], [228.4, "That's been happening for a long time, starting when he was young until now."], [233.7, "People continue to perceive him, have continued to perceive him as a child, right?"], [240.5, "It started in the past and it kept going for a while."], [243.7, "And then again, we talked about going to the gym: since last year, Jim has gone to the gym."], [250.6, "He has exercised every day, right?"], [253.8, "Starting last year up until now."], [257.3, "And then finally, we changed to the past tense because we're talking about one specific event."], [263.1, "The fight, right?"], [264.4, "That happened in the past."], [265.5, "It's over."], [266.2, "It was just a short event in the past: started, finished in the past, it's done."], [271.5, "It's not a long time period, it's very short and complete, so we use the simple past for that."], [277.8, "That's all you need to know about grammar."], [280.4, "Don't think too much about the grammar."], [282.8, "All right, on to version number three, into the future."], [286.1, "Okay, we can imagine this is my idea for a movie, and I'm telling you the story, what I think will happen in this movie."], [294.4, "Here's my movie idea, in the future, ten years from now."], [298.0, "Ten years from now, there will be a very small man named Jim."], [303.5, "Jim will only be one foot tall."], [306.3, "Even though he'll only be 48 years old, people will think he's a child."], [312.0, "People will perceive him as a child."], [315.4, "In the eyes of the public, Jim will be a cute little boy only."], [320.3, "Jim will hate this."], [321.7, "He's going to say, I want people to accept me as I really am."], [325.6, "I want them to give me unconditional respect."], [329.7, "I don't want people to go on treating me like a child."], [334.5, "Jim will go to the gym and exercise every day."], [338.1, "He'll become very strong."], [340.2, "He'll also learn kickboxing."], [342.6, "One day a tall man's gonna challenge him and laugh and say, you're such a cute little man."], [349.6, "Jim will get angry."], [351.6, "He'll yell and he'll kick the man."], [353.6, "They'll start fighting."], [354.4, "The fight is going to last 20 hours."], [358.9, "The men's hands and legs will become intertwined and they'll fall down."], [364.1, "Jim will finally break away from the man and then he'll jump up and kick him in the head."], [369.9, "Jim will win the fight and he'll yell."], [372.5, "No matter how you slice it, I just kicked your ass."], [383.8, "Okay, “going to” and “will”."], [385.9, "However, in normal speech, we do not say “going to” and “will”."], [391.0, "We change the pronunciation."], [392.7, "We say “'ll” instead of “will”."], [395.3, "We say Jim'll, Jim'll; the man'll, the man'll challenge him; Jim'll fight him."], [400.8, "We don't say “Jim will”, we say Jim'll, Jim'll."], [404.6, "We just add the “'ll” sound to the subject."], [408.5, "And the other thing we do: instead of “going to”, we say “gonna”."], [414.0, "Jim's gonna get angry."], [416.4, "Not Jim is going to get angry."], [420.3, "Jim's gonna."], [421.5, "Jim's, z, z, z, you need the z sound there."], [424.8, "Jim's gonna equals Jim is going to."], [429.8, "Jim's gonna."], [431.4, "All right, and that's how we actually use the future in normal speech."], [435.5, "So when you hear “gonna”, when you hear “'ll”, that means the future."], [441.5, "Okay, please go back, listen to each section, pause, and try to tell that version yourself."], [449.3, "Try to tell the story using the past 10 years ago."], [453.7, "Try it again with since last year, and then try it again in the future."], [458.9, "If you have trouble, if it's difficult, relax."], [461.9, "This takes time."], [462.9, "Just relax, go back, listen again, go back, listen again, listen, listen, listen very carefully."], [470.6, "Hear how the verbs change, hear how the vocabulary changes sometimes."], [476.3, "Listen carefully, that's the most important part."], [478.6, "Don't get upset if you can't tell the story yourself."], [481.6, "It's okay, that will take time."], [483.7, "Listening is the most important part."], [486.1, "Alright, I will see you next time."], [488.5, "Go on and listen to the commentary."], [490.7, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.0, "Hello, welcome to the commentary for Longtime Affair."], [5.9, "This is an interesting letter, I think."], [9.2, "So it's talking about, basically, two people."], [12.2, "They're married."], [13.7, "So there's a woman and she's married to somebody, a man, obviously."], [17.7, "And then there's a guy and he's also married."], [19.9, "But these two people are having an affair with each other."], [24.1, "And an affair is a relationship outside of marriage."], [29.1, "So if you have a girlfriend who's not your wife, that relationship is called an affair."], [36.3, "Now we're same with a woman or a man."], [38.3, "So they're having an affair."], [39.5, "It's been happening for a while."], [41.1, "So it's not a short thing."], [42.7, "It's a long-term thing."], [45.0, "And they love each other very, very deeply."], [49.2, "Unconditional love, they describe it."], [51.4, "Our roots are intertwined."], [53.5, "So their deep feelings are intertwined together."], [59.0, "But they're in their 50s, so they're older, and they don't want to leave their families."], [65.1, "Maybe they have children, probably adult children, and they don't want to destroy their families."], [71.7, "So this is kind of an interesting situation."], [75.4, "And I used this in my class here in San Francisco."], [79.7, "There was a very interesting discussion about this article, and I think there were a lot of different opinions, actually."], [87.8, "I was a little surprised."], [91.5, "So some people thought, oh, it's terrible."], [96.2, "They must end the affair, and they're doing a very, very bad thing."], [103.0, "I would say that would be the normal American reaction, the normal American opinion."], [109.4, "However, most of the students did not have that opinion."], [112.0, "And most of my students are Asian."], [114.5, "Japanese and Korean and Thai and most of them actually had very different ideas."], [120.7, "I would say about half of them said they should continue doing what they're doing but continue to be secret."], [129.2, "So they said, continue the affair, because they love each other very much, but they also love their families and don't want to hurt their families."], [136.5, "So they said these students said just continue doing what you are doing."], [142.0, "But, you know, keep it a secret so you don't hurt your families."], [146.6, "So just continue going."], [148.0, "And they thought that this is not so terrible, because these people love each other very much, and it's not horrible."], [155.4, "They're not bad people."], [157.2, "So that was another opinion."], [159.5, "Then a final opinion was that they should get a divorce each of them should divorce their."], [166.1, "Families, their spouses, and they should marry each other."], [171.8, "So they should stop this affair because they obviously love each other so much."], [176.1, "Maybe they don't have the same feeling for their wife or husband."], [179.1, "They should get divorced each of them and then marry each other."], [182.3, "And that was the third opinion."], [184.4, "And those two opinions, those last two, continue or get divorced, were definitely the most popular opinions in my class."], [191.3, "A little surprising to me."], [192.7, "And it showed me something that, you know, this idea is very cultural."], [199.6, "The idea of having affairs and the idea of what is good or bad in marriage has differences in different cultures."], [207.9, "Not that anybody thinks, you know, encourages affairs."], [211.7, "Nobody was saying, oh affairs are good."], [214.0, "Every husband and wife should have an affair."], [215.9, "Nobody said that."], [217.2, "But there were different attitudes about how is it terrible a little bit?"], [221.6, "Is it terrible?"], [222.7, "Really horrible?"], [224.0, "Bad?"], [225.1, "Is it not so bad?"], [226.8, "And that was very different."], [229.5, "Each individual had different opinions about that, and I could see different cultural ideas about that too."], [236.7, "A little bit later, maybe a couple weeks later, I was in the bookstore here in San Francisco down at Union Square, downtown."], [244.8, "And I saw a book about this subject."], [248.9, "This exact subject, the cultural ideas."], [253.1, "Cultural opinions, about having affairs in marriage."], [257.9, "And I didn't read the whole book."], [259.5, "I didn't want to buy it."], [260.8, "I just kind of skimmed it."], [262.5, "I read it quickly."], [263.5, "I read the summary and I skimmed through it quickly."], [266.1, "But I had the basic idea that it's true, that every country has different rules, different opinions about affairs, whether they are really, really bad or a little bad or if they're okay as long as they're secret or there are many different opinions."], [284.1, "It talked about how in Japan there are different opinions: that it's not horrible, but that it can be common among some men."], [292.9, "And how in other places, you know, they have the idea that if the man pays for sex with a prostitute, then it's not cheating, it's not an affair, because there's no emotional involvement."], [305.9, "And so some cultures think, oh, that's not so bad."], [309.9, "And other cultures think, oh, it's pretty normal for couples to have an affair with somebody else, but they should be very kind of secretive about it."], [320.9, "They shouldn't let everybody know, and it's not terrible."], [325.6, "And then it talked about in this book how America actually is quite different from much of the world, because in America the opinions are very strong, that affairs are horrible."], [335.0, "Terrible."], [336.1, "Almost evil."], [338.2, "And this is stronger than in most places in the world."], [344.1, "Many people have this idea, but in America this idea is very, very, very strong."], [348.6, "Stronger than in other countries."], [350.8, "So that was interesting to me, because when I chose this letter for my class, I thought everybody would agree: oh, this is bad, they should end it immediately."], [359.8, "They're really bad people."], [361.6, "Because I'm thinking like an American, I'm thinking that's what most Americans would say."], [366.6, "But in fact, it's not what most of my students said, not at all."], [370.5, "In fact, I think maybe only one student said something like that, and all the other ones were less judgmental, less strong about it."], [379.9, "So interesting, very interesting."], [381.3, "It shows again how culture can influence our ideas about this quite a bit, about many things, very basic things such as relationships are affected by culture."], [394.1, "And often it's in a subtle way."], [395.6, "It's not obvious sometimes."], [397.2, "It's a little more deep, those differences, but those differences are there."], [402.6, "And learning to communicate effectively is important so we can understand those differences."], [408.3, "And I don't think in these kind of cases, these kinds of situations, there's no right or wrong answer."], [417.8, "Right?"], [418.0, "God didn't write something down and we all must follow it."], [421.6, "I think that every culture has reasons for their beliefs, and there are good and bad points to those cultural beliefs."], [432.6, "And you know, I very much like this idea of not holding on to opinions too strongly, because we never really know, we can't ever really be sure about things."], [448.3, "So even if we have a strong opinion, it's good to remember that it's just an opinion."], [457.2, "And maybe it's good for us, but maybe other people in other situations."], [461.5, "In other cultures."], [462.8, "In other places."], [464.5, "With other circumstances."], [466.2, "Maybe our opinion is not good for them."], [469.2, "And it's always good to remember that."], [471.0, "I try to remember that I have strong opinions about things."], [474.2, "Certainly about education and teaching and about many things."], [477.4, "And sometimes they're too strong, and I have to remind myself: you know, AJ, it's just an opinion."], [485.3, "It's not right, it's not 100% correct."], [488.4, "Some God in heaven did not give you this opinion; it's just your opinion."], [494.5, "It's good for me, it's good for my experiences, but in the end, finally, it's only an opinion, and it's not good for everybody."], [505.0, "All right, but another issue about this letter."], [508.5, "This long time affair situation, is the issue of a double standard."], [514.8, "And this is something we also talked about in my class, and something that I feel very strongly about."], [521.6, "What's a double standard?"], [522.7, "We've had that phrase before."], [524.4, "A double standard is a rule that is different for different people."], [529.5, "For example, a rule that is different for women than it is for men."], [535.1, "And we see this double standard everywhere in the world about having affairs."], [542.2, "I'm sure you know and I'm sure you will agree that in most countries."], [547.5, "If a man has an affair."], [550.1, "It's less serious than if a woman has an affair, right?"], [554.4, "So a man is married and he has sex with another woman."], [557.0, "Maybe he pays a prostitute."], [558.9, "Maybe he has a girlfriend."], [561.8, "You know in different countries, we might think different things about this, but we might think this is bad."], [568.6, "But in most countries, and I want to say all countries, almost all countries, most people will still have a little bit of an attitude."], [579.5, "Oh, that's normal for men It's not so terrible."], [583.6, "He's a man But if we change the situation."], [587.3, "We have a woman, a wife, she's married."], [590.0, "She has an affair, she pays a man to have sex."], [593.3, "Or she has a boyfriend."], [596.3, "In most cultures, almost all, we will judge the woman much worse."], [601.2, "She's terrible, she's a prostitute, she's a slut, she's horrible."], [606.6, "Right?"], [607.3, "It's much worse, much more negative for the woman than for the man."], [613.3, "And that is a double standard."], [615.7, "I think it's wrong, I think it's a hundred percent wrong."], [620.1, "The woman, if she does something, she's terrible, horrible, everybody criticizes her and says she's a bad person."], [627.3, "But if a man does the same thing, oh, it's okay, it's not so bad, it's normal, or it's a little bad but it's not terrible."], [637.8, "And that is a clear double standard."], [640.6, "We see that in almost every country I know of."], [644.6, "In my class discussion, everybody agreed that in their own country this was a double standard."], [651.0, "In Thailand, if a man has an affair, it's less serious than if a woman does."], [657.5, "In Japan, same situation; in America, same."], [660.3, "I don't know about Europe; my guess is probably the same."], [664.7, "And that's not good. It shows that, to be honest, women are still not equal."], [670.7, "You're getting closer."], [672.4, "Especially in some countries, in the United States, women are getting much closer to being equal."], [677.6, "In Europe, I'm sure."], [679.9, "In Japan, in many countries."], [682.5, "But there's still a lot of work to do."], [685.4, "There's still so many double standards about women, where the woman is treated more badly, or she's judged more harshly, more severely, she's judged in a more negative way than a man for the exact same situation."], [703.5, "And of course we see this in working too, that women are getting more jobs, they're getting better and better jobs in the United States."], [711.1, "But still, if you look at the top."], [713.4, "The top of the company."], [715.2, "The president."], [716.2, "The CEO."], [717.2, "The very top officers."], [719.1, "They're still mostly men."], [720.5, "If you look at the American government, the senators, the Congress people, the president, of course, guess what?"], [729.4, "Mostly men still."], [731.2, "So we still have this double standard, but in politics, in business, in culture, everywhere."], [738.6, "So there's still a lot of work to do."], [740.0, "I think it's work that women have to do, but I think men also have to realize this."], [745.1, "And they have to understand it, and they need to help change it, because it's something that affects them as well."], [752.4, "You know, if you have a daughter, if you have a girlfriend, do you really want her to be treated badly?"], [759.6, "Do you really want her to have a double standard?"], [763.1, "I don't, and I hope you don't either."], [765.9, "So it's a big issue, this idea of double standard."], [769.3, "And I think that we see the double standard issue most strongly when it comes to sex."], [775.2, "Sexual relationships."], [776.5, "That's where women really get treated badly and they get judged differently and much more negative."], [783.4, "A man has sex with many women."], [785.8, "Oh, he's cool."], [787.8, "A woman has sex with many men."], [790.2, "Oh, she's a slut."], [791.4, "She's terrible."], [793.2, "Same situation."], [794.1, "The woman is treated very negatively, very badly."], [796.2, "The man is almost admired, almost complemented."], [800.7, "It's wrong, it's terrible."], [802.7, "And about affairs, as we just discussed, same thing."], [805.4, "A man has an affair, oh, it's not so bad."], [808.3, "A woman has an affair, terrible, terrible, terrible."], [811.6, "So this is a double standard that in the area of sex."], [814.7, "Even, I think we see this a lot with even enjoying sex."], [818.8, "Men are taught to enjoy sex."], [820.9, "If a man really likes sex a lot,"], [823.2, "it's great, and he's very passionate, then that's seen as wonderful: he's a passionate man."], [829.3, "But if a woman really enjoys sex, and she's very passionate and very direct about it, then sometimes she gets criticized a lot."], [838.6, "And so we see a lot of women who are afraid to enjoy sex, or afraid to say they enjoy sex; they're afraid people will criticize them."], [849.6, "Another double standard that we see with women, especially in this area of sexual relationships."], [855.7, "So anyway, those are the two big issues I wanted to talk about, one being the double standard that we see with women and men in most cultures, most societies."], [865.6, "And then the second thing was just the cultural differences from country to country,"], [870.5, "region to region, about this idea of having affairs."], [873.3, "How bad is it?"], [874.4, "Well, that depends on where you're from, it probably depends on your age, many different things."], [879.5, "All right, well, very interesting topic this time."], [882.2, "Hope you enjoyed it."], [883.7, "Remember, please help us out."], [885.3, "Go to Delicious, right?"], [887.4, "Go to Delicious and register, and then please go to effortlessenglish.com and tag us."], [897.7, "You go to our website and then you click the tag button that you downloaded after you registered."], [903.2, "And registering with Delicious is free, and it really helps our club."], [907.4, "It helps us a lot."], [908.1, "It will help us get new members, recruit new members without spending money for advertising."], [915.4, "It helps me keep the price low, low, low, so everyone can do it."], [921.5, "If necessary, in the future, I will advertise."], [925.2, "I will do more Google ads."], [928.1, "I will be more aggressive about marketing and trying to get more members because I want more members."], [935.4, "It gives more energy to the club."], [937.0, "Right, more people participating, it's more fun."], [937.5, "So I will do that in the future, if necessary."], [938.1, "I hope it's not necessary, because if I have to do that, I will have to raise the price."], [939.3, "So please help us out: go to Delicious, register, and then tag our websites."], [940.2, "All right, I'll see you next time."], [940.7, "Hope you enjoyed it, bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
