e more time, from the top."], [637.9, "s", "This time, if you want, if you want to practice speaking, I will pause after the key phrases."], [646.2, "s", "Please repeat them."], [648.4, "s", "When you repeat, copy my pronunciation, especially copy my intonation."], [654.9, "s", "When do I go up?"], [656.4, "s", "When do I go down?"], [658.1, "s", "And remember in English we start high, ah, and we drop, ah, ah."], [663.2, "s", "So listen for that and copy it exactly."], [666.1, "s", "Here we go."], [667.2, "s", "There was a girl named Tomoe."], [669.4, "s", "One day she took it upon herself to change her husband."], [678.1, "s", "One day she took it upon herself to change her husband."], [686.5, "s", "Very good."], [687.3, "s", "Tomoe was very picky."], [691.8, "s", "Tomoe was very picky."], [696.4, "s", "Good."], [697.1, "s", "She wanted the apartment to always be perfectly clean, but her husband was a lousy housekeeper."], [707.9, "s", "But her husband was a lousy housekeeper."], [712.7, "s", "Good."], [713.4, "s", "One day, Tomoe said, when you do the laundry, please sort the clothes by color."], [723.6, "s", "Very good."], [725.2, "s", "Please sort the clothes by color."], [729.9, "s", "Tomoe was very polite, but her husband took this the wrong way."], [740.5, "s", "But her husband took this the wrong way."], [747.0, "s", "Very good."], [747.7, "s", "He yelled, why are you criticizing me?"], [750.4, "s", "Why do you hate me?"], [752.2, "s", "I'm not a lousy husband."], [757.9, "s", "I'm not a lousy husband."], [762.7, "s", "Very good."], [763.6, "s", "Then he jumped up and down, pulled his hair, and said, I wash my hands of this."], [774.6, "s", "Good."], [775.3, "s", "I wash my hands of this."], [780.2, "s", "Very good."], [780.5, "s", "I wash my hands of this."], [783.1, "s", "I will never do laundry again."], [785.8, "s", "Okay, that is all."], [787.4, "s", "Now, please pause or stop this and try to tell all of the story yourself."], [795.7, "s", "Use all of the new phrases, all of the key phrases."], [800.4, "s", "And try to tell all of the story."], [802.8, "s", "If you can't, don't worry, relax, just listen again."], [807.4, "s", "Try to listen to it every day."], [809.6, "s", "See you next time, bye."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.4, "Hello, welcome to the Point of View mini-story for the Meddling Mother-in-Law lesson."], [7.4, "Let's get started."], [8.1, "In our first version of the story, we will start with the phrase “right now”."], [14.4, "The original story was in the past, so now we're going to start with “right now”."], [18.6, "Right now, there is a girl named Tomoe."], [24.3, "She takes it upon herself to change her husband."], [28.6, "Tomoe is very picky."], [31.1, "She wants the apartment to always be perfectly clean, but her husband is a lousy housekeeper."], [39.7, "One day, Tomoe says, when you do laundry, please sort the clothes by color."], [47.7, "Tomoe is very polite, but her husband takes this the wrong way."], [52.2, "He yells, why are you criticizing me?"], [55.0, "Why do you hate me?"], [56.2, "I'm not a lousy husband."], [57.5, "Then he jumps up and down, pulls his hair, and says, I wash my hands of this."], [65.0, "I will never do laundry again."], [70.0, "All right, very good."], [71.8, "Now let's change the story a little bit."], [74.1, "We're going to start the story with the phrase, since last April."], [79.7, "Starting in last April, continuing until now."], [83.3, "Since last April."], [83.9, "Ok, there's a girl named Tomoe."], [89.4, "Since last April, she has taken it upon herself to change her husband."], [97.3, "Since that time, Tomoe has been very, very picky."], [101.2, "She has wanted the apartment to always be perfectly clean."], [105.9, "But her husband has always been a lousy housekeeper."], [111.4, "One day, Tomoe said, when you do the laundry, please sort the clothes by color."], [119.6, "At that time, Tomoe was very polite, but her husband took it the wrong way."], [125.8, "He yelled, why are you criticizing me?"], [128.7, "Why do you hate me?"], [130.3, "I'm not a lousy husband."], [133.4, "Then he jumped up and down, pulled his hair and said, I wash my hands of this."], [139.6, "I will never do laundry again.\""], [144.6, "Okay, did you notice, again, this happens a lot when we begin something with the perfect tenses."], [150.6, "We often switch to another tense, often to the past tense."], [154.8, "So we talked about one day."], [158.2, "I'm sorry, I didn't say “one day”: Tomoe has taken it upon herself to change her husband."], [162.2, "It means she started trying to change him last April."], [166.6, "She has continued trying to change him until now or until this day where they had the argument."], [175.6, "It started in the past and it continued."], [178.4, "So we say, she has taken it upon herself, has taken."], [183.7, "And we say, Tomoe has been very picky."], [187.0, "This gives the idea that something changed."], [189.9, "Maybe in April something happened, because before April maybe she wasn't picky, but since April she has been very picky, starting in April until now."], [200.1, "You get the idea."], [201.7, "But then when I say, “One day, Tomoe said”, okay, “one day” is your clue."], [207.8, "“One day” tells you, aha, it happened and it's finished, so switch to the past tense."], [214.4, "All right, and now let's do our little... we can imagine we're telling a story about the future."], [221.7, "Maybe it's a movie idea, maybe it's any kind of story, but that's going to happen."], [226.7, "Here we go."], [228.3, "There will be a girl named Tomoe."], [231.9, "One day, in the future, she will take it upon herself to change her husband."], [237.7, "Tomoe will be very picky."], [241.0, "She'll want the apartment to always be perfectly clean, but her husband will be a lousy housekeeper."], [250.2, "One day, Tomoe will say, when you do laundry, please sort the clothes by color."], [256.2, "Tomoe will be very polite, but her husband will take it the wrong way."], [261.3, "He'll yell, why are you criticizing me?"], [264.3, "Why do you hate me?"], [265.7, "I'm not a lousy husband."], [267.8, "Then he'll jump up and down, pull his hair, and say, I wash my hands of this."], [273.4, "I'll never do laundry again."], [276.0, "Okay, in that story you heard, sometimes it's hard to hear the future, right?"], [283.3, "In the textbooks, they tell you to say “will”: he will do this, he will yell, I will go."], [293.2, "But in fact, when we speak, we don't usually say “will”."], [300.3, "Right, we combine it, we just say “'ll”."], [303.5, "There'll be a girl named Tomoe."], [306.6, "Right, there will be a girl."], [309.5, "There'll, there'll, there'll be a girl."], [313.6, "One day."], [315.1, "She'll take it upon herself, right, not she will."], [319.8, "She'll."], [321.0, "It's a contraction, We're putting the two sounds together."], [323.9, "Tomoe-o be very picky, right?"], [327.7, "Instead of saying, Tomoe will be very picky, we can say, Tomoe-o be very picky, right?"], [335.7, "We cut off the W-I."], [337.6, "Instead of saying, wi, we just say, ole."], [340.2, "Tomoe-o be very picky."], [342.5, "She'll want the apartment to be clean, always."], [346.4, "Not she will, she'll."], [348.1, "Her husbandel be a lousy housekeeper, not her husband will be."], [355.9, "Her husbandel, husbandel."], [359.3, "Now, this is not correct for writing."], [362.6, "With writing, we don't usually say husbandel."], [365.9, "But in speech, in conversation."], [369.7, "Especially native speakers speaking quickly."], [373.0, "They will say, ole, ole."], [375.5, "Her husband will be very bad."], [377.9, "Her husband will be about a bad housekeeper."], [381.3, "One day Tomoe will say, Tomoe will say, did you hear that?"], [385.7, "Tomoe will say."], [387.3, "Not Tomoe will say, Tomoe will say."], [391.4, "And then we switch to the present tense because it's a quote."], [396.1, "When you do laundry, please sort the clothes by color."], [398.8, "Tomoe will be very polite."], [400.4, "Tomoe will, to moe ol'."], [403.1, "Be very polite."], [405.6, "But her husband will take it the wrong way, her husband will take it the wrong way, he'll yell, not he will yell, he'll yell."], [413.8, "Why are you criticizing me, etc."], [416.5, "Then he'll jump up and down."], [419.5, "He'll pull his hair."], [422.0, "And he'll say... you can even do that: and he'll say."], [426.7, "And he'll say."], [428.2, "And he'll say,"], [430.4, "I wash my hands of this, I will never do laundry again."], [433.1, "So listen for that."], [434.1, "You know, the English you get in textbooks, in CD, on CDs, in schools."], [442.2, "It's a formal style of English."], [445.4, "It's also really a written kind of English."], [449.9, "So, you're learning to speak written English from these books, and, you know, that's okay, but it's not how we really speak."], [460.1, "It is not how Americans actually speak."], [464.0, "You'll never see it in a text, but: husband'll."], [466.3, "The husband'll be good."], [467.8, "The husband'll go to the store."], [470.1, "You'll never see that in a textbook, but in fact, that's exactly what we say every day: husband'll."], [476.6, "Tomoe'll."], [478.3, "He'll."], [480.2, "So listen for that."], [481.7, "When you listen to our movie lessons, when you listen to my commentaries,"], [485.9, "when you listen to these mini-stories, I'll try to use this more normal conversation style, so you can begin to understand it and use it."], [496.2, "Okay, that's all."], [496.8, "Well, as usual, listen to each version, then pause and try to tell the story yourself."], [505.4, "All of it, using the correct grammar, the correct verb tenses."], [510.4, "And try to use the correct pronunciation when you do this future one especially."], [515.1, "Try to use “'ll”, “'ll”, “'ll” instead of “will”, okay?"], [519.9, "See you next time."], [520.9, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.6, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for the Meddling Mother-in-Law lesson."], [5.1, "Let's get started."], [7.7, "This is a Dear Abby lesson, our first Dear Abby lesson."], [12.0, "Dear Abby is a very famous column in America."], [16.5, "And remember, a column is a newspaper article that you see repeatedly."], [21.9, "Maybe every day."], [23.5, "Maybe every month, maybe every week."], [26.4, "Dear Abby, I think it's every day."], [29.4, "And Abby, the original Abby, the first Abby, her name was Abigail Van Buren."], [35.5, "And I can't remember when she started, but like many, many years ago, 1960s."], [42.6, "Maybe 1950s, I'm not sure, but a long time ago."], [45.7, "And people write her letters."], [47.4, "They have a problem in their life."], [49.5, "They ask her for advice."], [50.9, "Abby, what should I do about my problem?"], [53.7, "And this has continued many, many, many years."], [56.8, "The first Abby died and now her daughter, I believe it's her daughter."], [61.9, "Continues the column, continues to write the column."], [65.2, "So now people write her, they still write Dear Abby, what should I do?"], [70.1, "So why?"], [70.8, "Why am I using Dear Abby on effortless English?"], [75.1, "Well, a couple of reasons."], [77.1, "The main reason, number one reason is that Dear Abby letters usually contain very conversational English."], [87.3, "People writing her, they don't write in a formal way, most of them."], [92.2, "They're writing in a conversational way, so they use a lot of idioms."], [97.0, "They use a little slang."], [99.0, "They use common conversational phrases, phrases we use in real conversations, phrases we use in real speech."], [109.9, "Phrases we use every day."], [111.9, "A lot of these phrases, you never see them in textbooks."], [115.4, "You never learn them in school."], [117.9, "Why?"], [118.4, "I don't know why."], [119.5, "Because they are very important."], [122.0, "I mean, if you want to communicate in English."], [125.4, "With a native speaker, you need to know these phrases."], [128.6, "We use them every single day."], [130.7, "This is not special slang."], [133.4, "This is, these are idioms, these are phrases we use all the time."], [138.7, "So I like that about Dear Abby."], [140.5, "Other newspaper articles are formal."], [143.6, "They use a written style of English, which is fine."], [147.8, "It's good to know that also."], [149.4, "But you also need to know the casual, everyday phrases that we use, and Dear Abby is a good place to learn them."], [157.2, "So another good thing about Dear Abby, my second point, they're short."], [161.1, "These are short letters, so you don't need to read a long, long letter."], [166.7, "However, they're short, but they have a lot of good stuff, a lot of good phrases."], [173.3, "Even though this letter is very, very short."], [175.8, "There are still several words and phrases we can learn from it."], [179.6, "So I like that."], [181.8, "And why do I like short?"], [183.7, "Well, I like short because it allows you to go deep."], [187.2, "Right?"], [187.9, "You can really focus on this little short article which will have maybe."], [194.0, "I don't know, it depends on your level."], [196.0, "But it will have at least one new phrase hopefully."], [198.9, "Maybe a few new phrases."], [201.7, "Maybe you know these phrases but you can't use them."], [204.8, "Maybe you kind of know them, I think I know it, but you never use them."], [208.9, "Well, by using something very short and simple, You can learn these new phrases."], [214.1, "You can practice them many, many, many times."], [216.3, "You can learn them deeply."], [218.1, "You can internalize them."], [219.6, "Remember that word?"], [220.6, "Internalize them."], [221.8, "You can learn them very deeply."], [223.7, "So that's another reason."], [225.0, "And reason number three."], [227.4, "Dear Abbey letters also have a nice bit of culture, a little bit of American culture."], [233.9, "You can see some common problems that American people, American families, American relationships have."], [242.8, "These people are writing about everyday problems."], [245.7, "Now, some are a little strange."], [248.1, "Some are quite normal."], [249.5, "This one is very normal, the meddling mother-in-law."], [253.4, "This is a problem probably many American wives might have."], [258.5, "In fact, another point for, I guess, is that, in fact, these are problems many people have in the world."], [265.4, "Not just America, right?"], [267.0, "A difficult mother-in-law, that's a problem that every country has."], [271.4, "People in all over the world, wives, have problems with their mother-in-laws."], [277.5, "And husbands also have problems with their mother-in-laws."], [279.8, "It's a common problem."], [281.1, "So I like that."], [281.7, "It connects you to everyday problems."], [285.5, "And that's also a nice way to learn, you can actually imagine these situations."], [291.6, "Finally, one last point why I like Dear Abby letters, why I'm using them."], [296.3, "They're great for discussion and forums because every letter, the person asks for advice."], [306.2, "What should I do?"], [308.3, "Well, Dear Abby, she writes her answer, but in effortless English, I will not include her answer."], [314.6, "Why not?"], [316.4, "Why don't I include Abby's answer?"], [319.0, "Because I want you to write your answer."], [322.6, "I want you to go to the forums where it says article essays and I want you to write what should this person do."], [331.0, "In your opinion, what should they do?"], [334.0, "Should she yell at her mother in law?"], [336.5, "Should she be quiet and think, be happy that her mother-in-law is helping her?"], [341.8, "Should she try to tell her in a polite way, please don't do my laundry?"], [347.7, "Is the mother-in-law the problem?"], [349.9, "Or is the wife the problem?"], [352.0, "Or is there another problem?"], [354.3, "Okay, all of these things, there's a lot of things you can write about with a very short Dear Abby letter."], [361.9, "Every letter the person says, what should I do?"], [364.8, "I want you to go to the forums and write, one paragraph maybe, what should the person do?"], [371.1, "In this case, what should the wife do about the mother-in-law?"], [376.6, "The mother-in-law is doing her laundry and cleaning the dishes, and the wife doesn't like it."], [385.1, "She's very picky."], [386.8, "So the wife says, what should I do?"], [389.5, "She's afraid if she says something, the mother-in-law will take it the wrong way."], [395.1, "Maybe she'll get angry and upset."], [397.3, "So what should she do?"], [399.0, "I don't know."], [399.4, "Now, go to the forums and write your opinion."], [402.1, "What should this woman do?"], [404.9, "So with Dear Abby letters also, I use them in my class here in San Francisco."], [409.8, "I use them really almost every day to try to teach real conversational phrases, not just formal written textbook English."], [423.4, "And in fact, some of my students are joining Effortless English to review."], [428.4, "So I use these letters in my class, then I make an effortless English lesson."], [433.9, "And my students in San Francisco can listen to the same lesson."], [438.5, "They had it in my class, and now they can review it again and again and again."], [442.1, "I hope that helps them."], [443.9, "For other members who don't live in San Francisco, it's okay."], [448.1, "You can listen as many times as you want."], [451.5, "That's why I love MP3s."], [453.8, "I love audio lessons."], [455.3, "To be honest, effortless English is a better way to learn English than my classes in San Francisco."], [467.1, "My classes in San Francisco, the students pay $300 a month or more."], [474.1, "You're paying, what, $50, $60, $77 for a year."], [480.2, "But I think you have a better deal."], [482.0, "I think you will learn English better than the people in my class."], [487.3, "Why?"], [488.9, "Well, simple."], [490.3, "Review and repetition."], [492.7, "Review and repetition."], [494.3, "My students in my class, they hear these lessons only one time."], [499.8, "So when I taught them the meddling mother-in-law letter, and they learned the new phrases."], [506.3, "You know, they enjoyed it."], [507.3, "We practiced it."], [508.1, "We did some mini stories, and then they went home, and they never looked at it again."], [515.5, "They never heard it again."], [517.6, "They never reviewed it again."], [519.9, "So what happened?"], [521.0, "Well, they forgot."], [522.0, "They forgot most of it."], [523.9, "How do I know they forgot?"], [525.6, "Because the next day I asked them, you know, what does take it upon yourself mean?"], [532.4, "And nobody knows."], [533.7, "And I asked them a week later, and I asked them, what does PIKI mean?"], [538.6, "And nobody knows."], [540.2, "They forgot."], [541.1, "Why did they forget?"], [542.5, "They forgot because they did not internalize the English."], [546.8, "They did not repeat it enough."], [549.3, "They did not review it enough."], [551.8, "They did not hear it enough times."], [556.0, "That's your advantage, using the internet, using MP3s, using your iPod, using your computer."], [563.6, "You can review and review and review as much as possible."], [569.2, "With effortless English, I encourage you."], [572.3, "With each lesson."], [573.7, "Listen to each part one time."], [577.8, "Maybe two times, every day."], [580.4, "For one week or for two weeks."], [584.3, "Maybe for three weeks."], [585.2, "I don't know."], [585.8, "It depends on your level."], [587.9, "If your very high level, maybe one week is enough."], [590.8, "If you're more of an intermediate level student, maybe you need a couple weeks, two or three weeks."], [596.8, "But learn it completely, okay?"], [599.7, "This is not a race."], [601.5, "If you do every lesson very, very fast, you prove nothing, okay?"], [608.2, "It just means you did everything fast and now you forgot everything and you didn't learn very much."], [613.9, "It's much better to go slowly and learn each lesson completely."], [622.6, "One time is not enough."], [624.5, "One day is not enough."], [626.8, "When you listen to the Meddling Mother-in-Law lesson,"], [630.7, "The audio."], [631.9, "Read the text."], [633.6, "Listen to the mini-stories."], [635.3, "Listen to the point of view mini-stories."], [637.5, "Listen to this commentary, listen to the vocabulary."], [639.8, "Doing it one time, one day, it's not enough, it's just not enough."], [646.3, "You have to listen to it today, and then tomorrow listen to it again, and the next day one more time, and the next day again one more time."], [660.8, "That's how you really learn the English deeply, so you can understand it instantly."], [667.8, "No hesitation, no thinking, you know it, you hear it, you know it."], [672.5, "That's also how you learn to use it instantly."], [676.1, "No thinking, no translating, no thinking in Japanese and then translating to English and then speaking, no."], [685.6, "You have to learn it very completely."], [688.5, "That means a lot of review."], [690.5, "You've got to listen to these lessons many times, many days."], [695.8, "When you do, trust me, please trust me, you will internalize the grammar."], [700.8, "You will learn it very deeply."], [702.5, "You will internalize the vocabulary."], [705.3, "You will internalize the pronunciation."], [708.5, "You will automatically begin to improve your vocabulary."], [713.6, "Your pronunciation."], [715.2, "The speed of your understanding, your listening comprehension speed."], [720.9, "Your speaking speed, your fluency."], [723.7, "And also your speaking pronunciation."], [726.0, "Everything will improve, but you must review, you must over-learn."], [731.1, "Please do that."], [731.9, "Please trust me."], [733.1, "If you over-learn each lesson."], [736.3, "If you do that for six months, eight months, one year."], [740.1, "You will be fluent in English, you will feel comfortable with English, you will improve a lot."], [746.6, "You will improve a lot more than people using normal methods, using textbooks, using schools."], [753.9, "I promise you this is not just me AJ Hogue giving you my opinion."], [759.0, "There is a lot of research about this."], [761.9, "Okay, enjoy the Dear Abby letters and I will see you next time."], [765.4, "Remember, overlearn, overlearn, overlearn."], [768.9, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["meddling", "/ˈmedlɪŋ/", "hay xen vào, can thiệp"], ["mother-in-law", "/ˈmʌðər ɪn lɔː/", "mẹ chồng, mẹ vợ"], ["wash your hands of", "/wɒʃ jɔː hændz ɒv/", "phủi tay, không dính dáng nữa"], ["politely", "/pəˈlaɪtli/", "một cách lịch sự"], ["laundry", "/ˈlɔːndri/", "đồ giặt; việc giặt giũ"], ["do the laundry", "/duː ðə ˈlɔːndri/", "giặt đồ"], ["bed rest", "/bed rest/", "nằm nghỉ tại giường"], ["due to", "/djuː tuː/", "do, vì"], ["pregnancy", "/ˈpreɡnənsi/", "việc mang thai"], ["I don't mind", "/aɪ dəʊnt maɪnd/", "tôi không phiền"], ["occasional", "/əˈkeɪʒənl/", "thỉnh thoảng"], ["load", "/ləʊd/", "một mẻ (đồ giặt)"], ["help out", "/help aʊt/", "giúp đỡ"], ["be over", "/bi ˈəʊvə/", "ghé sang nhà"], ["watch the kids", "/wɒtʃ ðə kɪdz/", "trông bọn trẻ"], ["picky", "/ˈpɪki/", "kén chọn, kỹ tính"], ["prefer", "/prɪˈfɜː/", "thích hơn"], ["put away", "/pʊt əˈweɪ/", "cất đi"], ["dishes", "/ˈdɪʃɪz/", "bát đĩa"], ["sort", "/sɔːt/", "phân loại"], ["take it upon yourself", "/teɪk ɪt əˈpɒn jɔːˈself/", "tự ý làm"], ["anyway", "/ˈeniweɪ/", "dù sao, vẫn cứ"], ["strong-willed", "/ˌstrɒŋ ˈwɪld/", "cứng đầu, ý chí mạnh"], ["respect", "/rɪˈspekt/", "tôn trọng"], ["parenting", "/ˈpeərəntɪŋ/", "việc nuôi dạy con"], ["take things the wrong way", "/teɪk θɪŋz ðə rɒŋ weɪ/", "hiểu lầm, phật ý"], ["dirty laundry", "/ˈdɜːti ˈlɔːndri/", "chuyện xấu trong nhà"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["ready to wash her hands of", "sẵn sàng phủi tay với"], ["How do I politely tell her to stop", "làm sao để lịch sự bảo bà thôi"], ["It all started when", "mọi chuyện bắt đầu khi"], ["on bed rest due to my pregnancy", "nằm nghỉ tại giường vì mang thai"], ["I didn't mind her doing an occasional load", "tôi không phiền khi bà thỉnh thoảng giặt một mẻ"], ["to help us out", "để giúp chúng tôi"], ["any time she's over to watch the kids", "lần nào bà sang trông bọn trẻ"], ["I'm very picky about", "tôi rất kỹ tính về"], ["the main reason I don't want her doing it", "lý do chính tôi không muốn bà làm"], ["puts things away in the wrong places", "cất đồ sai chỗ"], ["I wasn't done sorting it", "tôi chưa phân loại xong"], ["She took it upon herself to do it anyway.", "Vậy mà bà vẫn tự ý làm."], ["She's very strong-willed.", "Bà rất cứng đầu."], ["not respecting our parenting", "không tôn trọng cách chúng tôi nuôi dạy con"], ["She often takes things the wrong way.", "Bà hay hiểu lầm ý người khác."], ["What's the best way to", "cách tốt nhất để ... là gì"], ["her help is not needed", "không cần bà giúp"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["How do I + politely + V?", "How do I politely say no to my boss?", "Làm sao để tôi lịch sự từ chối sếp?", "how do i"], ["S + tell + someone + to stop + V-ing", "I told him to stop calling me.", "Tôi bảo anh ta thôi gọi cho tôi.", "stop"], ["It all started when + clause", "It all started when I moved to Hanoi.", "Mọi chuyện bắt đầu khi tôi chuyển ra Hà Nội.", "all started"], ["... due to + noun", "The flight was cancelled due to the storm.", "Chuyến bay bị hủy do bão.", "due to"], ["I don't mind + someone + V-ing", "I don't mind you using my laptop.", "Tôi không phiền khi bạn dùng laptop của tôi.", "don't mind|didn't mind"], ["any time + clause", "Call me any time you need help.", "Gọi tôi bất cứ lúc nào bạn cần giúp.", "any time|anytime"], ["S + be + picky about + noun", "My son is picky about food.", "Con trai tôi kén ăn.", "picky about"], ["S + prefer + someone + V ... than ...", "I prefer you stay home than go out tonight.", "Tôi muốn bạn ở nhà hơn là ra ngoài tối nay.", "prefer"], ["S + be + not done + V-ing", "I'm not done eating yet.", "Tôi chưa ăn xong.", "done"], ["S + took it upon + oneself + to V", "He took it upon himself to fix the car.", "Anh ấy tự ý sửa xe.", "upon himself|upon herself|upon myself"], ["S + have had problems with + noun/V-ing", "We have had problems with the neighbours.", "Chúng tôi gặp rắc rối với hàng xóm.", "problems with"], ["S + take(s) things the wrong way", "Please don't take this the wrong way.", "Đừng hiểu lầm ý tôi nhé.", "wrong way"], ["What's the best way (for us) to + V?", "What's the best way to learn English?", "Cách tốt nhất để học tiếng Anh là gì?", "best way"]]$j$::jsonb
)
